{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "def largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n.\"\"\"\n    # The algorithm computes the smallest prime factor (spf) and returns n // spf.\n    # If n is prime, its spf is n itself, and the largest proper divisor is 1.\n\n    limit = int(n**0.5)\n\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return n // 2\n\n    f = 3\n    while f <= limit:\n        if n % f == 0:\n            return n // f\n        f += 2\n\n    # If no factors were found, n must be a prime number.\n    return 1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "import math\n\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n.\n    It iterates up to the square root of n to find the smallest factor, then returns n divided by that factor.\n    \"\"\"\n    for i in range(2, int(math.isqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return n // i\n    return 1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return list of prime factors of given integer in ascending order,\n    each listed corresponding to its multiplicity in the factorization.\n    \"\"\"\n    factors = []\n    # Factor out all occurrences of 2 from n.\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        factors.append(2)\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Check for odd factors starting from 3 up to the square root of n.\n    p = 3\n    max_p = math.isqrt(n) + 1\n    while p <= max_p and n > 1:\n        while n % p == 0:\n            factors.append(p)\n            n //= p\n            # Recompute max_p since n has decreased.\n            max_p = math.isqrt(n) + 1\n        p += 2 # Increment p by 2 to check only odd numbers.\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be the last remaining prime factor.\n    if n > 1:\n        factors.append(n)\n    return factors\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/23", "solution": "To implement the provided software design specification, the code will be structured into multiple files within a `src/stringutils/` directory, along with configuration files like `pyproject.toml`, `requirements.txt`, `README.md`, and `Dockerfile`.\n\nHere is the complete code based on the detailed design:\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/__init__.py\n\"\"\"stringutils package exports core functionality.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\n# Configure basic logging for the package\nlogging.basicConfig(level=os.environ.get(\"STRINGUTILS_LOG_LEVEL\", \"INFO\").upper(),\n                    format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\nfrom .repository import SQLiteMetricsRepository, MetricsRepository\nfrom .services import StringService\nfrom .api import create_app\nfrom .cli import main as cli_main\n\ndef strlen(value: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the length of the given string, using the core service.\n    This also increments the 'service_direct' metric.\n    \"\"\"\n    repo: MetricsRepository = SQLiteMetricsRepository()\n    service = StringService(repo)\n    return service.strlen(value)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/models.py\n\"\"\"Data transfer objects for string operations.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidStringError\nfrom . import utils\n\nclass StringDTO:\n    \"\"\"DTO for string input, ensuring type and basic validity.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: str) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"StringDTO must be initialized with a string.\")\n        self.value = value\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_str(cls, value: Any) -> \"StringDTO\":\n        \"\"\"Factory method to create a DTO from a potentially non-string input.\"\"\"\n        string_value = utils.to_str(value)\n        return cls(string_value)\n\n    def validate(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates the DTO's string value.\n        Currently, this method does not perform additional validation as `from_str`\n        already ensures the value is a valid string.\n        \"\"\"\n        pass\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/services.py\n\"\"\"Business logic for string operations.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .models import StringDTO\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidStringError\nfrom . import utils\nfrom .repository import MetricsRepository\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass StringService:\n    \"\"\"Provides core string operations and integrates with metrics.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repo: MetricsRepository) -> None:\n        self._repo = repo\n\n    def strlen(self, value: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the length of a string, validating input and updating metrics.\"\"\"\n        s = utils.to_str(value) # Converts to str and raises InvalidStringError for None/unconvertible\n        length = len(s)\n        try:\n            self._repo.incr_count(\"service_direct\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Metrics update failed for 'service_direct': {e}\")\n        return length\n\n    def strlen_dto(self, dto: StringDTO) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes string length using a StringDTO, ensuring validation through DTO.\"\"\"\n        dto.validate() # Call DTO's validation method\n        length = len(dto.value)\n        try:\n            self._repo.incr_count(\"service_direct\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Metrics update failed for 'service_direct' (DTO call): {e}\")\n        return length\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/controllers.py\n\"\"\"Interface adapters for CLI and HTTP API to call service methods.\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Tuple\n\nfrom .services import StringService\nfrom .repository import MetricsRepository\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidStringError\nfrom .models import StringDTO\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Controller for handling command-line interface requests.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: StringService, repo: MetricsRepository) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n        self._repo = repo\n\n    def _print_usage(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Prints CLI usage information to stderr.\"\"\"\n        sys.stderr.write(\"Usage: stringutils strlen <string>\\n\")\n        sys.stderr.write(\"  <string>  The string for which to compute the length.\\n\")\n        sys.stderr.write(\"Example: stringutils strlen \\\"hello world\\\"\\n\")\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the CLI command based on provided arguments.\"\"\"\n        exit_code = 0\n        try:\n            if len(argv) < 3 or argv[1] != \"strlen\":\n                self._print_usage()\n                exit_code = 1\n                return exit_code\n\n            input_string = argv[2]\n            length = self._service.strlen(input_string)\n            print(length)\n            exit_code = 0\n        except InvalidStringError as e:\n            sys.stderr.write(f\"Error: Invalid string input: {e}\\n\")\n            exit_code = 2\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred during CLI execution.\")\n            sys.stderr.write(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\\n\")\n            exit_code = 3\n        finally:\n            try:\n                self._repo.incr_count(\"cli\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to increment CLI metric: {e}\")\n        return exit_code\n\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Controller for handling HTTP API requests.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: StringService, repo: MetricsRepository) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n        self._repo = repo\n\n    def post_strlen(self, json_body: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[Dict[str, Any], int]:\n        \"\"\"Handles the POST /strlen API request to compute string length.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            if not json_body or \"value\" not in json_body:\n                return {\"error\": \"Missing 'value' field in JSON request body.\"}, 400\n\n            input_value = json_body[\"value\"]\n            string_dto = StringDTO.from_str(input_value)\n            length = self._service.strlen_dto(string_dto)\n\n            return {\"length\": length}, 200\n        except InvalidStringError as e:\n            return {\"error\": str(e)}, 400\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred during API call to /strlen.\")\n            return {\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}, 500\n        finally:\n            try:\n                self._repo.incr_count(\"api_post_strlen\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to increment API metric: {e}\")\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/repository.py\n\"\"\"Persistence abstraction and implementations for usage metrics.\"\"\"\n\nimport sqlite3\nimport datetime\nimport logging\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nimport os\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nDEFAULT_DB_PATH = \"stringutils_metrics.db\"\nMETRICS_TABLE_SCHEMA = \"\"\"\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS metrics (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    endpoint TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n    count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    last_updated TIMESTAMP NOT NULL\n)\n\"\"\"\nMETRICS_INDEX_ENDPOINT = \"CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_metrics_endpoint ON metrics(endpoint)\"\nMETRICS_INDEX_LAST_UPDATED = \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_metrics_last_updated ON metrics(last_updated)\"\n\n\nclass MetricsRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class for metrics persistence.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def incr_count(self, endpoint: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Increment the call count for a given endpoint.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def get_count(self, endpoint: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Retrieve the current call count for an endpoint.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def prune_older_than(self, days: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Remove metric entries older than a specified number of days.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n\nclass SQLiteMetricsRepository(MetricsRepository):\n    \"\"\"SQLite implementation of the MetricsRepository.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str = DEFAULT_DB_PATH) -> None:\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._conn: sqlite3.Connection | None = None\n        self._initialize_db()\n\n    def _get_conn(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"Returns an active SQLite connection, opening it if necessary.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn is None:\n            self._conn = sqlite3.connect(self._db_path)\n            self._conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n        return self._conn\n\n    def _initialize_db(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the metrics table and indexes exist.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            conn = self._get_conn()\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(METRICS_TABLE_SCHEMA)\n            cursor.execute(METRICS_INDEX_ENDPOINT)\n            cursor.execute(METRICS_INDEX_LAST_UPDATED)\n            conn.commit()\n            logger.info(f\"SQLite metrics database initialized at {self._db_path}\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Error initializing SQLite database at {self._db_path}: {e}\")\n\n    def incr_count(self, endpoint: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Increments the count for the specified endpoint.\"\"\"\n        now = datetime.datetime.utcnow().isoformat(timespec='seconds')\n        try:\n            conn = self._get_conn()\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO metrics (endpoint, count, last_updated)\n                VALUES (?, 1, ?)\n                ON CONFLICT(endpoint) DO UPDATE SET\n                    count = count + 1,\n                    last_updated = ?;\n                \"\"\",\n                (endpoint, now, now)\n            )\n            conn.commit()\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to increment metric for endpoint '{endpoint}': {e}\")\n\n    def get_count(self, endpoint: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves the count for the specified endpoint.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            conn = self._get_conn()\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT count FROM metrics WHERE endpoint = ?\", (endpoint,))\n            result = cursor.fetchone()\n            return result[\"count\"] if result else 0\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to retrieve metric for endpoint '{endpoint}': {e}\")\n            return 0\n\n    def prune_older_than(self, days: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Deletes metric entries older than 'days' from now.\"\"\"\n        if days < 0:\n            logger.warning(\"Prune days cannot be negative. Skipping pruning.\")\n            return\n\n        cutoff_date = datetime.datetime.utcnow() - datetime.timedelta(days=days)\n        try:\n            conn = self._get_conn()\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"DELETE FROM metrics WHERE last_updated < ?\", (cutoff_date.isoformat(timespec='seconds'),))\n            conn.commit()\n            logger.info(f\"Pruned metrics older than {days} days. Rows deleted: {cursor.rowcount}\")\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to prune metrics: {e}\")\n\n    def close(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Closes the SQLite database connection.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn:\n            self._conn.close()\n            self._conn = None\n            logger.info(f\"SQLite connection to {self._db_path} closed.\")\n\n\nclass InMemoryMetricsRepository(MetricsRepository):\n    \"\"\"In-memory implementation of the MetricsRepository, useful for testing.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._store: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n\n    def incr_count(self, endpoint: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Increments the count for the specified endpoint.\"\"\"\n        now = datetime.datetime.utcnow()\n        entry = self._store.get(endpoint, {\"count\": 0, \"last_updated\": now})\n        entry[\"count\"] += 1\n        entry[\"last_updated\"] = now\n        self._store[endpoint] = entry\n\n    def get_count(self, endpoint: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves the count for the specified endpoint.\"\"\"\n        return self._store.get(endpoint, {}).get(\"count\", 0)\n\n    def prune_older_than(self, days: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Removes metric entries older than a specified number of days.\"\"\"\n        if days < 0:\n            logger.warning(\"Prune days cannot be negative. Skipping pruning.\")\n            return\n\n        cutoff_date = datetime.datetime.utcnow() - datetime.timedelta(days=days)\n        endpoints_to_prune = [\n            ep for ep, data in self._store.items()\n            if data.get(\"last_updated\") and data[\"last_updated\"] < cutoff_date\n        ]\n        for ep in endpoints_to_prune:\n            del self._store[ep]\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/utils.py\n\"\"\"Utility functions for string operations and validation.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidStringError\n\ndef validate_string(value: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is a valid string.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(value, str)\n\ndef to_str(value: Any) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts a value to a string, raising InvalidStringError if not convertible or None.\"\"\"\n    if value is None:\n        raise InvalidStringError(\"Input value cannot be None.\")\n    try:\n        return str(value)\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise InvalidStringError(f\"Could not convert input to string: {e}\") from e\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"Domain-specific exceptions.\"\"\"\n\nclass InvalidStringError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a string input is invalid or not convertible.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/api.py\n\"\"\"Flask application factory for the HTTP API.\"\"\"\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request, jsonify\nimport os\nimport logging\n\nfrom .controllers import APIController\nfrom .repository import SQLiteMetricsRepository, MetricsRepository\nfrom .services import StringService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidStringError\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef create_app(service: StringService | None = None, repo: MetricsRepository | None = None) -> Flask:\n    \"\"\"Factory function to create and configure the Flask application.\"\"\"\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n\n    _repo = repo or SQLiteMetricsRepository()\n    _service = service or StringService(_repo)\n    api_controller = APIController(_service, _repo)\n\n    @app.route(\"/strlen\", methods=[\"POST\"])\n    def post_strlen_endpoint():\n        \"\"\"HTTP POST endpoint to compute string length.\"\"\"\n        if not request.is_json:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Content-Type must be application/json\"}), 400\n        \n        json_body = request.get_json()\n        body, status_code = api_controller.post_strlen(json_body)\n        return jsonify(body), status_code\n\n    @app.errorhandler(InvalidStringError)\n    def handle_invalid_string_error(e):\n        \"\"\"Handle InvalidStringError by returning a 400 Bad Request.\"\"\"\n        logger.warning(f\"InvalidStringError caught by global handler: {e}\")\n        return jsonify({\"error\": str(e)}), 400\n\n    @app.errorhandler(Exception)\n    def handle_generic_error(e):\n        \"\"\"Handle all other unexpected exceptions by returning a 500 Internal Server Error.\"\"\"\n        logger.exception(\"An unhandled exception occurred during API request.\")\n        return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}), 500\n\n    @app.before_first_request\n    def setup_pruning():\n        \"\"\"Performs metrics pruning before the first request.\"\"\"\n        retention_days = int(os.environ.get(\"STRINGUTILS_METRICS_RETENTION_DAYS\", 90))\n        if retention_days > 0:\n            logger.info(f\"Attempting to prune metrics older than {retention_days} days.\")\n            try:\n                _repo.prune_older_than(retention_days)\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to perform initial metrics pruning: {e}\")\n\n    return app\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringutils/cli.py\n\"\"\"CLI entrypoint for stringutils commands.\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\nfrom .repository import SQLiteMetricsRepository, InMemoryMetricsRepository, MetricsRepository\nfrom .services import StringService\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef main(argv: List[str] | None = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Main entrypoint for the stringutils CLI application.\"\"\"\n    full_argv = argv if argv is not None else sys.argv\n\n    use_in_memory_repo = os.environ.get(\"STRINGUTILS_USE_IN_MEMORY_METRICS\", \"false\").lower() == \"true\"\n    \n    repo: MetricsRepository\n    if use_in_memory_repo:\n        logger.info(\"Using InMemoryMetricsRepository for CLI.\")\n        repo = InMemoryMetricsRepository()\n    else:\n        logger.info(\"Using SQLiteMetricsRepository for CLI.\")\n        repo = SQLiteMetricsRepository()\n    \n    service = StringService(repo)\n    controller = CLIController(service, repo)\n\n    return controller.run(full_argv)\n\n```\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"stringutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nauthors = [\n  { name=\"Your Name\", email=\"your.email@example.com\" },\n]\ndescription = \"A simple package to compute string length with CLI and HTTP API.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nkeywords = [\"string\", \"utility\", \"cli\", \"api\", \"metrics\"]\nlicense = { text = \"MIT License\" }\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Development Status :: 3 - Alpha\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"Topic :: Utilities\",\n]\ndependencies = [\n    \"Flask>=2.0.0\",\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/stringutils\"\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/yourusername/stringutils/issues\"\n\n[project.scripts]\nstringutils = \"stringutils.cli:main\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n```\n\n```\n# requirements.txt\nFlask>=2.0.0\ngunicorn>=20.1.0\n```\n\n```markdown\n# String Utilities Package\n\nThis project provides a simple Python package for computing the length of a string,\nexposed via a Python function, a command-line interface (CLI), and an HTTP API.\nIt also captures basic usage metrics.\n\n## Features\n\n-   `strlen(value: str) -> int`: A direct Python function to get string length.\n-   `stringutils strlen <string>`: A CLI command for shell integration.\n-   `POST /strlen`: An HTTP API endpoint for service consumers.\n-   Usage metrics captured in a local SQLite database.\n-   Built with Python 3.9+, Flask, and SQLite.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install the package using `pip` from the project directory:\n\n```bash\npip install .\n```\n\nOr, if you prefer to install in editable mode for development:\n\n```bash\npip install -e .\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Python Library\n\n```python\nfrom stringutils import strlen\n\nlength = strlen(\"Hello, World!\")\nprint(f\"Length: {length}\")\n\nlength_empty = strlen(\"\")\nprint(f\"Length of empty string: {length_empty}\")\n\ntry:\n    strlen(None)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\n### Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\n```bash\n# Get the length of a string\nstringutils strlen \"Hello CLI\"\n\n# Handle spaces by quoting the string\nstringutils strlen \"Another String With Spaces\"\n\n# Invalid input (e.g., missing argument)\nstringutils strlen\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nThe HTTP API runs a Flask application.\n\n**To run the API (for development):**\n\n```bash\n# Using the package's create_app\npython -m flask --app stringutils.api run\n```\n\n**To run the API (production with Gunicorn):**\n\n```bash\ngunicorn \"stringutils.api:create_app()\" --bind 0.0.0.0:8000\n```\n\nOnce the API is running (e.g., on `http://localhost:5000`), you can call it:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"value\": \"API Test String\"}' \\\n     http://localhost:5000/strlen\n\n# Test with invalid input (missing 'value' field)\ncurl -X POST \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"invalid_field\": \"test\"}' \\\n     http://localhost:5000/strlen\n```\n\n## Metrics\n\nUsage metrics (call counts) are stored in `stringutils_metrics.db` (SQLite).\nMetrics are collected for: `cli`, `api_post_strlen`, `service_direct`.\nMetrics older than 90 days are pruned automatically when the API application starts.\nThis retention period can be configured via the `STRINGUTILS_METRICS_RETENTION_DAYS` environment variable.\n\n```bash\nexport STRINGUTILS_METRICS_RETENTION_DAYS=30\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 stringutils/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py         # Package exports, version\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py           # Data models (StringDTO)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py         # Business logic (StringService)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 controllers.py      # CLI and API controllers\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 repository.py       # Metrics persistence (SQLite, In-memory)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py            # Helper functions\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py       # Custom exceptions\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 api.py              # Flask app factory\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 cli.py              # CLI entrypoint\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/                      # (Not generated by prompt)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml              # Project metadata and build config\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 requirements.txt            # Runtime dependencies\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md                   # This file\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 Dockerfile                  # Containerization instructions\n```\n\n### Setting up Development Environment\n\n1.  **Clone the repository:**\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/yourusername/stringutils.git\n    cd stringutils\n    ```\n\n2.  **Create a virtual environment:**\n    ```bash\n    python -m venv .venv\n    source .venv/bin/activate\n    ```\n\n3.  **Install dependencies:**\n    ```bash\n    pip install -e .\n    ```\n\n## Dockerization\n\nA `Dockerfile` is provided for containerizing the HTTP API.\n\n```dockerfile\n# Dockerfile\n# Use a slim Python base image\nFROM python:3.9-slim-buster\n\n# Set the working directory in the container\nWORKDIR /app\n\n# Copy the dependency files first to leverage Docker cache\nCOPY requirements.txt .\n\n# Install dependencies\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt\n\n# Copy the entire source code\nCOPY src/ ./src/\nCOPY pyproject.toml .\n\n# Expose the port the app runs on\nEXPOSE 8000\n\n# Set environment variable for Flask app\nENV FLASK_APP=stringutils.api\n\n# Command to run the application using Gunicorn\nCMD [\"gunicorn\", \"stringutils.api:create_app()\", \"--bind\", \"0.0.0.0:8000\", \"--workers\", \"4\", \"--log-level\", \"info\"]\n\n```\n\nTo build and run the Docker image:\n\n```bash\ndocker build -t stringutils-app .\ndocker run -p 8000:8000 stringutils-app\n```\n```"}
