{"task_id": "HumanEval/28", "solution": "To implement the software design specification, the following files will be generated under the `src/strutils/` directory, along with `pyproject.toml` and `README.md` in the project root.\n\n```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# Packaging/build config (name, version, deps, entry-points)\n[project]\nname = \"strutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Small string utilities: concatenate list of strings\"\nauthors = [{name=\"Author\", email=\"dev@example.com\"}]\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\n\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"strutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Small string utilities: concatenate list of strings\"\nauthors = [\"Author <dev@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \"^3.8\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^7.0\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nstrconcat = \"strutils.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core>=1.0.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n## strutils\n\nA small Python library and CLI tool for concatenating lists of strings.\n\n### Installation (with poetry)\n\n```bash\npoetry add strutils\n```\n\n### CLI Usage\n\nConcatenate strings provided as arguments:\n```bash\nstrconcat hello world\n# Output: helloworld\n```\n\nConcatenate strings from standard input, one per line:\n```bash\necho -e \"first\\nsecond\\nthird\" | strconcat\n# Output: firstsecondthird\n```\n\n### Library Usage\n\n```python\nfrom strutils.services import StringConcatenator\nfrom strutils.controllers import ConcatenateController\nfrom strutils.exceptions import ValidationError\n\n# Using the core service\nconcatenator = StringConcatenator()\nresult_str = concatenator.concatenate([\"alpha\", \"beta\"])\nprint(f\"Service result: {result_str}\") # Output: Service result: alphabeta\n\ntry:\n    concatenator.concatenate([\"num\", 123])\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Service error: {e}\") # Output: Service error: Element at index 1 is not a string: int\n\n# Using the controller (provides structured output)\ncontroller = ConcatenateController(service=concatenator)\nsuccess_response = controller.concatenate_request([\"hello\", \" \", \"world\"])\nprint(f\"Controller success: {success_response}\") # Output: Controller success: {'result': 'hello world', 'count': 3}\n\nerror_response = controller.concatenate_request([\"test\", None])\nprint(f\"Controller error: {error_response}\") # Output: Controller error: {'error': 'Element at index 1 is not a string: NoneType'}\n```\n```\n\n---\n**File structure:**\n\n```\nsrc/\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 strutils/\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 controllers.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 cli.py\n```\n\n---\n**File contents:**\n\n### `src/strutils/exceptions.py`\n```python\nclass ValidationError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for input validation errors.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Return the error message as string representation.\"\"\"\n        return self.message\n```\n\n### `src/strutils/utils.py`\n```python\nfrom typing import Any, Iterable\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass ValidationUtils:\n    \"\"\"Provides utility methods for validating inputs.\"\"\"\n\n    def ensure_is_list_of_strings(self, strings: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that input is an iterable of strings.\n        Raises ValidationError if validation fails.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(strings, Iterable) or isinstance(strings, (str, bytes)):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input must be an iterable of strings (not a single string).\")\n        for idx, item in enumerate(strings):\n            if not self._is_string(item):\n                raise ValidationError(f\"Element at index {idx} is not a string: {type(item).__name__}\")\n\n    def _is_string(self, obj: Any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Internal helper to check if an object is a string.\"\"\"\n        return isinstance(obj, str)\n```\n\n### `src/strutils/models.py`\n```python\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom .utils import ValidationUtils\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass StringListDTO:\n    \"\"\"Data Transfer Object for a list of strings input.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, items: List[str]) -> None:\n        self.items = items\n\n    def validate(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates the stored list of strings using ValidationUtils.\"\"\"\n        validator = ValidationUtils()\n        validator.ensure_is_list_of_strings(self.items)\n\nclass ConcatenateResult:\n    \"\"\"Data Transfer Object for the concatenation operation result.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, result: str, count: int) -> None:\n        self.result = result\n        self.count = count\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Converts the result object to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\"result\": self.result, \"count\": self.count}\n```\n\n### `src/strutils/services.py`\n```python\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .utils import ValidationUtils\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass StringConcatenator:\n    \"\"\"Core service for concatenating a list of strings.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, encoding: str = \"utf-8\") -> None:\n        self.encoding = encoding\n        self._validator = ValidationUtils()\n\n    def concatenate(self, strings: List[str]) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Validates and concatenates a list of strings into a single string.\n        Returns an empty string for an empty list.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._validator.ensure_is_list_of_strings(strings)\n        return self._join(strings)\n\n    def _join(self, strings: List[str]) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Internal method to perform the actual string joining.\"\"\"\n        return ''.join(strings)\n```\n\n### `src/strutils/controllers.py`\n```python\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom .services import StringConcatenator\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .models import ConcatenateResult\n\nclass ConcatenateController:\n    \"\"\"API/controller layer to wrap string concatenation functionality.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, service: StringConcatenator) -> None:\n        self.service = service\n\n    def concatenate_request(self, strings: List[str]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Processes a concatenation request, handles errors, and returns a structured response.\n        Returns a dictionary with 'result' and 'count' or an 'error' message.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            result_str = self.service.concatenate(strings)\n            result_dto = ConcatenateResult(result=result_str, count=len(strings))\n            return result_dto.to_dict()\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            return {\"error\": str(e)}\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Catch unexpected errors to provide a generic failure message\n            return {\"error\": f\"An unexpected error occurred: {str(e)}\"}\n```\n\n### `src/strutils/cli.py`\n```python\nimport sys\nimport argparse\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom .controllers import ConcatenateController\nfrom .services import StringConcatenator\n\nclass CLIApp:\n    \"\"\"Command-line interface application for string concatenation.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, controller: ConcatenateController, prog_name: str = \"strconcat\") -> None:\n        self.controller = controller\n        self.prog_name = prog_name\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Main entry point for the CLI application.\n        Parses arguments, processes request, and prints output.\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=self.prog_name,\n            description=\"Concatenate a list of strings from arguments or stdin.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"strings\",\n            nargs=\"*\",\n            help=\"Strings to concatenate. If none provided, reads from stdin.\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n\n        input_strings: List[str]\n        if args.strings:\n            input_strings = args.strings\n        else:\n            input_strings = self._read_stdin_lines()\n\n        response: Dict[str, Any] = self.controller.concatenate_request(input_strings)\n\n        if \"error\" in response:\n            print(f\"Error: {response['error']}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2  # Exit code for validation errors\n        else:\n            print(response[\"result\"])\n            return 0  # Success exit code\n\n    def _read_stdin_lines(self) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Reads newline-separated lines from standard input.\"\"\"\n        return [line.rstrip('\\n') for line in sys.stdin]\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Entry point function for the console script.\"\"\"\n    service = StringConcatenator()\n    controller = ConcatenateController(service=service)\n    app = CLIApp(controller=controller)\n    return app.run(sys.argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n### `src/strutils/__init__.py`\n```python\n\"\"\"\nstrutils: A small Python library and CLI for string concatenation.\nThis module exports the main components for easy access.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .models import StringListDTO, ConcatenateResult\nfrom .utils import ValidationUtils\nfrom .services import StringConcatenator\nfrom .controllers import ConcatenateController\nfrom .cli import CLIApp, main as cli_main # Export cli_main for console scripts\n```"}
