sult['median']}, Count: {result['count']}\")\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e.message}, Details: {e.errors}\")\n\n# From a CSV file\n# Assuming 'data.csv' exists with numeric data\ntry:\n    result = api.compute({\"csv_path\": \"data.csv\", \"column\": 0})\n    print(f\"CSV Median: {result['median']}, Count: {result['count']}\")\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"CSV Error: {e.message}, Details: {e.errors}\")\n```\n\n### FastAPI Server (Optional)\n\nTo run the FastAPI server, ensure you have installed it with the `server` extra:\n`pip install \"stats-median[server]\"`\n\nThen, run:\n```bash\nuvicorn stats_median.server:create_app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nAccess at `http://localhost:8000/median` with a POST request.\n\nExample POST request payload:\n```json\n{\n  \"values\": [3, 1, 2, 4, 5]\n}\n```\nOr:\n```json\n{\n  \"csv_path\": \"/path/to/your/data.csv\",\n  \"column\": 0\n}\n```\n\n## Development\n\nThe project uses Poetry for dependency management.\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies\npoetry install\n\n# Run tests\npoetry run pytest\n\n# Run CLI via poetry\npoetry run median-cli --values \"1 2 3\"\n```\n```\n# src/stats_median/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nStats Median package provides a library and tools for median computation.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .calculator import MedianCalculator\nfrom .validators import InputValidator\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .repository import ListRepository\nfrom .api import MedianAPI\nfrom .cli import CLI # CLI is typically run as a script, but can be imported for testing\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_COLUMN, DEFAULT_PRECISION\n\n# Optional FastAPI server components\ntry:\n    from .server import create_app\nexcept ImportError:\n    create_app = None # type: ignore\n    # print(\"FastAPI server components not available. Install with 'server' extra.\")\n```\n\n```\n# src/stats_median/config.py\n\"\"\"\nConfiguration constants and default values for the median calculation package.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\n# Default column index for CSV files (0-based)\nDEFAULT_COLUMN: int = 0\n\n# Default precision for displaying median results\nDEFAULT_PRECISION: int = 6\n\n# Allowed types for direct numeric conversion\nALLOWED_TYPES: tuple[Any, ...] = (int, float)\n```\n\n```\n# src/stats_median/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nCustom exception types for the stats_median package.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any, Optional, List, Tuple\n\nclass ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised for invalid input data.\n    Attributes:\n        message -- explanation of the error\n        errors -- list of (index, value) tuples for offending elements\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, errors: Optional[List[Tuple[int, Any]]] = None) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n        self.errors = errors\n```\n\n```\n# src/stats_median/calculator.py\n\"\"\"\nCore median computation logic for validated numeric sequences.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Sequence, List\n\nclass MedianCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides methods to compute the median of a sequence of numeric values.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def compute(values: Sequence[float]) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the median of a sequence of float values.\n        Raises ValueError if the sequence is empty.\n        \"\"\"\n        vals: List[float] = list(values)\n        if not vals:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cannot compute median of empty sequence\")\n        vals.sort()\n        return MedianCalculator._median_of_sorted(vals)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _median_of_sorted(sorted_vals: List[float]) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the median from an already sorted list of float values.\n        Handles both odd and even length lists.\n        \"\"\"\n        n = len(sorted_vals)\n        mid = n // 2\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            return float(sorted_vals[mid])\n        return (sorted_vals[mid - 1] + sorted_vals[mid]) / 2.0\n```\n\n```\n# src/stats_median/validators.py\n\"\"\"\nInput validation utilities for coercing various input types into list[float].\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Sequence, Any, List, Tuple\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .config import ALLOWED_TYPES\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates and coerces input data to a list of floats.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_numeric_sequence(data: Sequence[Any]) -> List[float]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates an input sequence, coercing elements to float.\n        Raises ValidationError for empty input or non-numeric elements.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not data:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input sequence is empty.\")\n\n        result: List[float] = []\n        errors: List[Tuple[int, Any]] = []\n\n        for i, v in enumerate(data):\n            try:\n                result.append(InputValidator._coerce_to_float(v, i))\n            except ValueError:\n                errors.append((i, v))\n\n        if errors:\n            error_message = f\"Found {len(errors)} non-numeric value(s) in input.\"\n            raise ValidationError(error_message, errors=errors)\n\n        return result\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _coerce_to_float(value: Any, index: int) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Coerces a single value to float.\n        Raises ValueError if coercion is not possible.\n        \"\"\"\n        if isinstance(value, ALLOWED_TYPES):\n            return float(value)\n        if isinstance(value, str):\n            try:\n                return float(value.strip())\n            except ValueError:\n                pass # Fall through to raise generic ValueError\n        raise ValueError(f\"Cannot coerce value at index {index}: {value!r}\")\n```\n\n```\n# src/stats_median/repository.py\n\"\"\"\nFile I/O adapters for loading numeric sequences from CSV and saving results.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport csv\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom .validators import InputValidator\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass ListRepository:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles file operations like loading data from CSV and saving results.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def load_csv(path: str, column: int = 0, delimiter: str = ',') -> List[float]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Loads numeric values from a specified column in a CSV file.\n        Raises FileNotFoundError, PermissionError, or ValidationError.\n        \"\"\"\n        values_as_strings: List[str] = []\n        with open(path, newline='', encoding='utf-8') as fh:\n            reader = csv.reader(fh, delimiter=delimiter)\n            for i, row in enumerate(reader):\n                if i == 0 and not any(row): # Skip empty header row if present\n                    continue\n                try:\n                    cell_value = row[column]\n                    values_as_strings.append(cell_value)\n                except IndexError:\n                    raise ValidationError(f\"Missing column {column} on row {i+1} in CSV: {row!r}\", errors=[(i, row)])\n        \n        # Use InputValidator to robustly convert and validate all collected values\n        return InputValidator.validate_numeric_sequence(values_as_strings)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def save_result(path: str, result: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Saves a result dictionary to a file as JSON.\n        Performs an atomic write by using a temporary file.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            temp_path = path + '.tmp'\n            with open(temp_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as fh:\n                json.dump(result, fh, indent=2)\n            os.replace(temp_path, path) # Atomic rename\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Clean up temp file if something went wrong\n            if os.path.exists(temp_path):\n                os.remove(temp_path)\n            raise IOError(f\"Failed to save result to {path}: {e}\") from e\n```\n\n```\n# src/stats_median/cli.py\n\"\"\"\nCommand-line interface (CLI) for the median calculation package.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional, Union\n\nfrom .repository import ListRepository\nfrom .validators import InputValidator\nfrom .calculator import MedianCalculator\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_COLUMN, DEFAULT_PRECISION\n\nclass CLI:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles command-line argument parsing and orchestration of median computation.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Entrypoint for the CLI. Parses arguments, performs computation, and prints results.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for error).\n        \"\"\"\n        ns = self._parse_args(argv)\n\n        try:\n            values: List[float]\n            if ns.csv:\n                values = ListRepository.load_csv(ns.csv, column=ns.column)\n            elif ns.values:\n                # If --values is provided, it can be a single string or multiple arguments\n                if isinstance(ns.values, list): # e.g., --values 1 2 3\n                    tokens = [str(x) for x in ns.values]\n                else: # e.g., --values \"1 2 3\"\n                    tokens = ns.values.split() if isinstance(ns.values, str) else []\n                values = InputValidator.validate_numeric_sequence(tokens)\n            else:\n                # Should be caught by argparse (requires --values or --csv)\n                # but as a fallback, raise error.\n                raise ValidationError(\"Either --values or --csv must be provided.\")\n\n            median = MedianCalculator.compute(values)\n            result = {\"median\": median, \"count\": len(values)}\n\n            if ns.output:\n                ListRepository.save_result(ns.output, result)\n\n            self._print_result(result, precision=ns.precision)\n            return 0\n\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            if e.errors:\n                print(\"Details of invalid inputs:\", file=sys.stderr)\n                for idx, val in e.errors:\n                    print(f\"  Index {idx}: {val!r}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except FileNotFoundError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: File not found - {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except PermissionError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Permission denied - {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n    def _parse_args(self, argv: List[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses command-line arguments using argparse.\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Compute the median of a numeric sequence.\"\n        )\n        group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n        group.add_argument(\n            \"--values\",\n            nargs=\"+\", # Allows \"1 2 3\" or --values 1 --values 2\n            help=\"Space-separated list of numeric values (e.g., '1 2 3' or 1 2 3)\",\n        )\n        group.add_argument(\n            \"--csv\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Path to a CSV file containing numeric values.\",\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--column\",\n            type=int,\n            default=DEFAULT_COLUMN,\n            help=f\"0-based column index to read from CSV (default: {DEFAULT_COLUMN}).\",\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--precision\",\n            type=int,\n            default=DEFAULT_PRECISION,\n            help=f\"Decimal places for median output (default: {DEFAULT_PRECISION}).\",\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--output\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Optional path to save the result as a JSON file.\",\n        )\n\n        return parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n\n    def _print_result(self, result: dict, precision: int = DEFAULT_PRECISION) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Prints the median result to stdout.\n        \"\"\"\n        median_value = result.get(\"median\")\n        count_value = result.get(\"count\")\n        if median_value is not None:\n            print(f\"Median: {median_value:.{precision}f}\")\n        if count_value is not None:\n            print(f\"Count: {count_value}\")\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the median-cli console script.\n    \"\"\"\n    cli = CLI()\n    sys.exit(cli.run(sys.argv))\n\n```\n\n```\n# src/stats_median/api.py\n\"\"\"\nProgrammatic API adapter for median computation, returning structured results.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence, Union\nfrom .validators import InputValidator\nfrom .calculator import MedianCalculator\nfrom .repository import ListRepository\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass MedianAPI:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides a programmatic interface to compute the median.\n    Accepts a payload with values or a CSV path.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def compute(self, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Union[float, int]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the median based on the provided payload.\n        Payload can contain \"values\" (Sequence[Any]) or \"csv_path\" (str).\n        Raises ValidationError for invalid input.\n        \"\"\"\n        values: Sequence[float]\n        column: int = payload.get(\"column\", 0)\n\n        if \"csv_path\" in payload:\n            csv_path = payload[\"csv_path\"]\n            if not isinstance(csv_path, str):\n                raise ValidationError(\"csv_path must be a string.\")\n            values = ListRepository.load_csv(csv_path, column=column)\n        elif \"values\" in payload:\n            raw_values = payload[\"values\"]\n            if not isinstance(raw_values, (list, tuple, Sequence)):\n                 raise ValidationError(\"values must be a list or sequence.\")\n            values = InputValidator.validate_numeric_sequence(raw_values)\n        else:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Payload must contain either 'values' or 'csv_path'.\")\n\n        median = MedianCalculator.compute(values)\n        return {\"median\": median, \"count\": len(values)}\n```\n\n```\n# src/stats_median/server.py\n\"\"\"\nOptional FastAPI server adapter for exposing the median computation API via HTTP.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\nfrom typing import List, Optional, Union, Any\n\n# Conditional import to handle optional dependency\ntry:\n    from .api import MedianAPI\n    from .exceptions import ValidationError\n    from .config import DEFAULT_COLUMN\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    # This block handles cases where the core logic isn't installed\n    # or if there's a problem during a partial install.\n    # For FastAPI to function, the core parts are essential.\n    # If the \"server\" extra is not installed, this file would not be used.\n    # This is mainly a defensive check.\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Core median calculation components failed to load for server: {e}\")\n\nclass MedianRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"\n    Pydantic model for the request payload to the /median endpoint.\n    Requires either 'values' or 'csv_path'.\n    \"\"\"\n    values: Optional[List[Any]] = Field(\n        None,\n        description=\"A list of numeric values (integers or floats) to compute the median for.\"\n    )\n    csv_path: Optional[str] = Field(\n        None,\n        description=\"Absolute path to a CSV file containing numeric data. Requires filesystem access.\"\n    )\n    column: int = Field(\n        DEFAULT_COLUMN,\n        description=f\"0-based column index to read from the CSV file (default: {DEFAULT_COLUMN}).\"\n    )\n\n    model_config = {\n        \"json_schema_extra\": {\n            \"examples\": [\n                {\n                    \"values\": [3, 1, 2, 4, 5]\n                },\n                {\n                    \"csv_path\": \"/path/to/data.csv\",\n                    \"column\": 0\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n    }\n\n    def model_post_init(self, __context: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Custom validation to ensure either values or csv_path is provided.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.values is None and self.csv_path is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"Either 'values' or 'csv_path' must be provided.\")\n        if self.values is not None and self.csv_path is not None:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cannot provide both 'values' and 'csv_path'.\")\n\n\nclass FastAPIServer:\n    \"\"\"\n    A wrapper class for the FastAPI application.\n    \"\"\"\n    app: FastAPI\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.app = create_app()\n\ndef create_app() -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates and configures the FastAPI application.\n    Exposes /median and /health endpoints.\n    \"\"\"\n    app = FastAPI(\n        title=\"Median Calculator API\",\n        description=\"API for computing the median of numeric sequences.\",\n        version=\"0.1.0\",\n    )\n    api_service = MedianAPI() # Instantiate the core API service\n\n    @app.get(\"/health\", summary=\"Health check endpoint\")\n    async def health_check():\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns a simple status to indicate the API is operational.\n        \"\"\"\n        return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n    @app.post(\"/median\", response_model=Dict[str, Union[float, int]], summary=\"Compute the median of a numeric sequence\")\n    async def compute_median_endpoint(request_data: MedianRequest):\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the median of a list of numbers provided directly or from a CSV file.\n        Returns the median and the count of valid numbers.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            # Convert Pydantic model to a dictionary suitable for MedianAPI.compute\n            payload = request_data.model_dump(exclude_unset=True)\n            result = api_service.compute(payload)\n            return result\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=400,\n                detail={\"message\": e.message, \"errors\": e.errors}\n            )\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=500,\n                detail={\"message\": f\"An internal server error occurred: {e}\"}\n            )\n\n    return app\n```\n\n```\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: Python CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [ main ]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [ main ]\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n    - name: Install Poetry\n      run: |\n        curl -sSL https://install.python-poetry.org | python -\n    - name: Add Poetry to PATH\n      run: |\n        echo \"$HOME/.poetry/bin\" >> $GITHUB_PATH\n    - name: Configure Poetry for project\n      run: |\n        poetry config virtualenvs.in-project true\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        poetry install --with dev,server --no-interaction --no-root\n    - name: Install project itself (for imports)\n      run: |\n        poetry install --no-deps\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: |\n        poetry run pytest\n```\n\n```\n# tests/test_calculator.py\n# Unit tests are forbidden, so this file is empty.\n# If allowed, this would contain tests for MedianCalculator.\n```\n\n```\n# tests/test_validators.py\n# Unit tests are forbidden, so this file is empty.\n# If allowed, this would contain tests for InputValidator.\n```\n\n```\n# tests/test_repository.py\n# Unit tests are forbidden, so this file is empty.\n# If allowed, this would contain tests for ListR