{"task_id": "HumanEval/51", "solution": "Here is the complete executable code based on the provided software design specification.\n\n```\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"remove-vowels-lib\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A small, well-tested, reusable Python library that removes vowels from input text.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"remove_vowels_lib\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.8\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^7.0\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nremove-vowels = \"remove_vowels_lib:main_cli\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n```\n# requirements.txt\npytest>=7.0.0\n```\n```\n# README.md\n# remove-vowels-lib\n\nA small, well-tested, reusable Python library that removes vowels from input text.\nIt offers both a programmatic API and a command-line interface (CLI) for file and stream processing.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install remove-vowels-lib\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library API\n\n```python\nfrom remove_vowels_lib import remove_vowels, RemoveVowelsService\n\n# Using the convenience function\ntext = \"Hello, World! This is a test.\"\nresult = remove_vowels(text)\nprint(result) # Output: Hll, Wrld! Ths s  tst.\n\n# Using the service class for more control (e.g., custom vowel sets)\nservice = RemoveVowelsService(vowels={'a', 'o', 'u'}) # Only 'a', 'o', 'u' are removed\nresult_custom = service.process(\"Hello, World! This is a test.\")\nprint(result_custom) # Output: Hell, Wrld! Ths is  test.\n```\n\n### Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nThe CLI can read from standard input or a file, and write to standard output or a file.\n\n```bash\n# Process text from stdin and print to stdout\necho \"Hello, World!\" | remove-vowels\n# Output: Hll, Wrld!\n\n# Process an input file and write to stdout\nremove-vowels -i input.txt\n# Output: (content of input.txt with vowels removed)\n\n# Process an input file and write to an output file\nremove-vowels -i input.txt -o output.txt\n\n# Process with a custom set of vowels (case-insensitive by default for ASCII)\nremove-vowels -i input.txt --vowels \"aeiouy\"\n\n# Process large files in chunks (default chunk size is 4096 bytes)\nremove-vowels -i large_file.txt -o processed_large_file.txt --chunk-size 8192\n```\n\n## Features\n\n- **Programmatic API**: `remove_vowels(text: str)` function and `RemoveVowelsService` class.\n- **CLI**: `remove-vowels` command for file and stream processing.\n- **Streaming**: `FileProcessor` for efficient handling of large files.\n- **Configurable**: Custom vowel sets and chunk sizes.\n- **Robust Error Handling**: Specific exceptions for invalid inputs and IO issues.\n\n## Development\n\nTo set up the development environment:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/your-repo/remove-vowels-lib.git\ncd remove-vowels-lib\npoetry install\npoetry run pytest\n```\n```\n# .gitignore\n# Byte-code files\n*.pyc\n__pycache__/\n\n# Distribution / packaging\n.venv/\nbuild/\ndist/\n*.egg-info/\n\n# Editors\n.vscode/\n.idea/\n*.swp\n*~\n\n# Misc\n.DS_Store\n```\n```\n# src/remove_vowels_lib/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nremove_vowels_lib package exports.\nProvides the core function, service class, and CLI entry point.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .core import remove_vowels, RemoveVowelsService\nfrom .cli import CLIController\n\n__all__ = [\"remove_vowels\", \"RemoveVowelsService\", \"CLIController\"]\n\ndef main_cli(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    CLI entry point for the 'remove-vowels' console script.\n    \"\"\"\n    return CLIController().run(argv)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main_cli(sys.argv[1:])\n\n```\n```\n# src/remove_vowels_lib/config.py\n\"\"\"\nConfiguration module for default values and a Config dataclass.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Iterable, Optional, frozenset as frozenset_type\n\nDEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE: int = 4096\n\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates runtime configuration, including vowel set and chunk size.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, vowels: Optional[Iterable[str]] = None, chunk_size: int = DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(chunk_size, int) or chunk_size <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Chunk size must be a positive integer, got {chunk_size}\")\n        self.chunk_size: int = chunk_size\n        self.vowels: frozenset_type[str] = frozenset_type(vowels) if vowels is not None else frozenset_type() # Utils.build_vowel_set will handle actual building with defaults\n        # Note: The design stated Config __init__ would validate vowel entries,\n        # but Utils.build_vowel_set is designed for this.\n        # This implementation lets Config store an iterable (or empty frozenset)\n        # which Utils.build_vowel_set can then process.\n        # Alternatively, Config could directly call Utils.build_vowel_set here:\n        # from .utils import Utils\n        # self.vowels: frozenset_type[str] = Utils.build_vowel_set(vowels)\n\n```\n```\n# src/remove_vowels_lib/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nDomain-specific exceptions for the remove_vowels_lib.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass VowelProcessingError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Base exception for errors during vowel processing or file operations.\n    Wraps underlying exceptions for consistent error reporting.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, cause: Optional[Exception] = None) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n        self.cause = cause\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        if self.cause:\n            return f\"{self.message} (Caused by: {self.cause})\"\n        return self.message\n\n```\n```\n# src/remove_vowels_lib/utils.py\n\"\"\"\nUtility module for low-level text filtering, validation, and vowel set building.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Any, Iterable, Set, frozenset as frozenset_type\n\nclass Utils:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides stateless helper methods for validation and text manipulation.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_text_input(text: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates that the input is a string.\n        Raises TypeError if the input is not a string.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(text, str):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Input must be a string, got {type(text).__name__}.\")\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _is_single_char(ch: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Internal helper to check if a character is a single-character string.\n        \"\"\"\n        return isinstance(ch, str) and len(ch) == 1\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def build_vowel_set(vowels: Optional[Iterable[str]] = None) -> frozenset_type[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Normalizes a provided vowel list (or default) to a frozenset of characters.\n        Includes both lowercase and uppercase variants for ASCII if default is used.\n        Raises ValueError if any entry in the custom vowels is not a single character.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Default vowels are defined in core.py, importing here to avoid circular dependency if core imported utils directly.\n        # For simplicity and to avoid circular import if DEFAULT_VOWELS is in core,\n        # define default here or ensure a safe import path.\n        # Let's assume DEFAULT_VOWELS (with both cases) can be imported from core.\n        from .core import DEFAULT_VOWELS # Deferred import to break potential cycle\n\n        if vowels is None:\n            return DEFAULT_VOWELS\n        else:\n            processed_vowels = set()\n            for v_char in vowels:\n                if not Utils._is_single_char(v_char):\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Custom vowel set must contain single-character strings, got '{v_char}'\")\n                processed_vowels.add(v_char)\n            return frozenset_type(processed_vowels)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def filter_text(text: str, vowel_set: Set[str]) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Removes all characters present in the given vowel_set from the text.\n        \"\"\"\n        return \"\".join(char for char in text if char not in vowel_set)\n\n```\n```\n# src/remove_vowels_lib/core.py\n\"\"\"\nCore module providing the RemoveVowelsService class and the top-level remove_vowels function.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Iterable, Optional, frozenset as frozenset_type\nfrom .utils import Utils\nfrom .exceptions import VowelProcessingError\n\n# Default ASCII vowels, including both uppercase and lowercase for convenience\nDEFAULT_VOWELS: frozenset_type[str] = frozenset({'a','e','i','o','u','A','E','I','O','U'})\n\nclass RemoveVowelsService:\n    \"\"\"\n    A stateless service for removing vowels from text, configurable with custom vowel sets.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, vowels: Optional[Iterable[str]] = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the service with a specified vowel set or the default.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._vowel_set: frozenset_type[str] = Utils.build_vowel_set(vowels)\n\n    def process(self, text: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Removes characters matching the service's configured vowel set from the input text.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            Utils.validate_text_input(text)\n            return Utils.filter_text(text, self._vowel_set)\n        except TypeError as e:\n            raise e # TypeError is expected to be raised directly as per FR1\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise VowelProcessingError(f\"Failed to process text due to an unexpected error.\", cause=e)\n\ndef remove_vowels(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    A convenience function to remove vowels from text using the default vowel set.\n    \"\"\"\n    service = RemoveVowelsService()\n    return service.process(text)\n\n```\n```\n# src/remove_vowels_lib/file_processor.py\n\"\"\"\nModule for streaming file processing, handling input/output files or stdin/stdout.\n\"\"\"\nimport io\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Callable, Iterator, Optional\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE\nfrom .exceptions import VowelProcessingError\n\nclass FileProcessor:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles streaming processing of files or standard I/O.\n    Reads input in chunks, applies a processor function, and writes output incrementally.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, chunk_size: int = DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the FileProcessor with a specified chunk size.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(chunk_size, int) or chunk_size <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Chunk size must be a positive integer, got {chunk_size}\")\n        self._chunk_size = chunk_size\n\n    def _read_in_chunks(self, file_stream: io.TextIOBase) -> Iterator[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Yields chunks of text from an opened text stream.\n        \"\"\"\n        while True:\n            chunk = file_stream.read(self._chunk_size)\n            if not chunk:\n                break\n            yield chunk\n\n    def process_file(self, input_path: Optional[str], output_path: Optional[str], processor: Callable[[str], str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Processes text from input_path (or stdin) and writes to output_path (or stdout).\n        \"\"\"\n        input_stream: io.TextIOBase\n        output_stream: io.TextIOBase\n\n        try:\n            if input_path:\n                input_stream = open(input_path, 'r', encoding='utf-8')\n            else:\n                input_stream = sys.stdin\n\n            if output_path:\n                output_stream = open(output_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8')\n            else:\n                output_stream = sys.stdout\n\n            with input_stream, output_stream:\n                for chunk in self._read_in_chunks(input_stream):\n                    processed_chunk = processor(chunk)\n                    output_stream.write(processed_chunk)\n        except FileNotFoundError as e:\n            raise VowelProcessingError(f\"Input file not found: {input_path}\", cause=e)\n        except PermissionError as e:\n            raise VowelProcessingError(f\"Permission denied for file operation on '{e.filename}'\", cause=e)\n        except IOError as e:\n            raise VowelProcessingError(f\"An I/O error occurred during file processing: {e}\", cause=e)\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Catch any other unexpected exceptions from the processor or internal logic\n            raise VowelProcessingError(f\"An unexpected error occurred during processing: {e}\", cause=e)\n\n```\n```\n# src/remove_vowels_lib/cli.py\n\"\"\"\nCommand-line interface controller for the remove_vowels_lib.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .core import RemoveVowelsService\nfrom .file_processor import FileProcessor\nfrom .config import Config, DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE\nfrom .exceptions import VowelProcessingError\nfrom .utils import Utils # For parsing custom vowels from CLI\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates command-line argument parsing and delegates processing\n    to RemoveVowelsService and FileProcessor.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the CLIController. Dependencies are created during run() based on args.\n        \"\"\"\n        pass # No injected dependencies at init for CLI, they are created in run()\n\n    def _parse_args(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> argparse.Namespace:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses command-line arguments using argparse.\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Removes vowels from text, supporting file and stream processing.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"-i\", \"--input\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Path to the input file. If omitted, reads from stdin.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"-o\", \"--output\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Path to the output file. If omitted, writes to stdout.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--chunk-size\",\n            type=int,\n            default=DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE,\n            help=f\"Chunk size (in characters) for streaming file processing. Default: {DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE}.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--vowels\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Custom string of characters to consider as vowels (e.g., 'aeiouAEIOU'). Overrides default vowels.\"\n        )\n        return parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    def run(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the CLI logic: parses arguments, sets up components, and processes text.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for failure).\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            args = self._parse_args(argv)\n\n            # Build vowel set based on CLI arg, fallback to default\n            custom_vowel_chars = None\n            if args.vowels:\n                custom_vowel_chars = [char for char in args.vowels]\n\n            # Build the specific vowel set for the service\n            vowel_set_for_service = Utils.build_vowel_set(custom_vowel_chars)\n            \n            # Create service and file processor instances\n            service = RemoveVowelsService(vowels=vowel_set_for_service)\n            file_processor = FileProcessor(chunk_size=args.chunk_size)\n\n            # Process the file/stream\n            file_processor.process_file(args.input, args.output, service.process)\n\n            return 0  # Success\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, VowelProcessingError) as e:\n            # Specific domain errors or invalid arguments\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Catch all other unexpected errors\n            print(f\"An unexpected fatal error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n\n```\n```\n# examples/example_usage.py\n\"\"\"\nExample usage demonstrating both library API and programmatic CLI invocation.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport os\nfrom io import StringIO\nfrom contextlib import redirect_stdout, redirect_stderr\n\n# Library API examples\nfrom src.remove_vowels_lib.core import remove_vowels, RemoveVowelsService\nfrom src.remove_vowels_lib.cli import CLIController\nfrom src.remove_vowels_lib.file_processor import FileProcessor\nfrom src.remove_vowels_lib.config import DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE\n\ndef run_library_examples():\n    print(\"--- Library API Examples ---\")\n\n    # 1. Using the convenience function `remove_vowels`\n    text1 = \"Hello, World! This is a test.\"\n    result1 = remove_vowels(text1)\n    print(f\"Original: '{text1}'\\nRemoved:  '{result1}'\\n\")\n\n    # 2. Using `RemoveVowelsService` with default vowels\n    service_default = RemoveVowelsService()\n    text2 = \"Programming is fun and challenging.\"\n    result2 = service_default.process(text2)\n    print(f\"Original: '{text2}'\\nRemoved (default vowels): '{result2}'\\n\")\n\n    # 3. Using `RemoveVowelsService` with custom vowels (e.g., remove 'a', 'o', 'u' only)\n    service_custom = RemoveVowelsService(vowels={'a', 'o', 'u', 'A', 'O', 'U'})\n    text3 = \"Python is an amazing language.\"\n    result3 = service_custom.process(text3)\n    print(f\"Original: '{text3}'\\nRemoved (custom aou):    '{result3}'\\n\")\n\n    # 4. Edge case: empty string\n    text4 = \"\"\n    result4 = remove_vowels(text4)\n    print(f\"Original: '{text4}'\\nRemoved:  '{result4}'\\n\")\n\n    # 5. Edge case: string with only vowels\n    text5 = \"aeiouAEIOU\"\n    result5 = remove_vowels(text5)\n    print(f\"Original: '{text5}'\\nRemoved:  '{result5}'\\n\")\n\n    # 6. Edge case: non-ASCII characters (preserved)\n    text6 = \"\u3053\u3093\u306b\u3061\u306f\u4e16\u754c\uff01Caf\u00e9\"\n    result6 = remove_vowels(text6)\n    print(f\"Original: '{text6}'\\nRemoved:  '{result6}'\\n\")\n\n\ndef run_cli_examples():\n    print(\"\\n--- CLI Examples (Programmatic Invocation) ---\")\n\n    # Prepare dummy files for CLI tests\n    input_file_path = \"input_example.txt\"\n    output_file_path = \"output_example.txt\"\n    large_input_file_path = \"large_input_example.txt\"\n\n    try:\n        with open(input_file_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(\"This is a sample text file.\\n\")\n            f.write(\"It has multiple lines.\\n\")\n            f.write(\"Vowels should be removed.\")\n\n        with open(large_input_file_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(\"A\" * 1000 + \"E\" * 1000 + \"B\" * 1000 + \"\\n\")\n            f.write(\"I\" * 1000 + \"O\" * 1000 + \"C\" * 1000 + \"\\n\")\n            f.write(\"U\" * 1000 + \"D\" * 1000 + \"F\" * 1000 + \"\\n\")\n\n\n        # 1. CLI: Input file to output file (default vowels)\n        print(\"1. CLI: input.txt -> output.txt (default vowels)\")\n        cli = CLIController()\n        exit_code = cli.run(['-i', input_file_path, '-o', output_file_path])\n        print(f\"CLI exit code: {exit_code}\")\n        if exit_code == 0:\n            with open(output_file_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                content = f.read().strip()\n                print(f\"Output content: '{content}'\\n\")\n        else:\n            print(\"CLI failed.\\n\")\n\n        # 2. CLI: Stdin to stdout (custom vowels 'a', 'e', 'y')\n        print(\"2. CLI: stdin -> stdout (custom vowels 'aey')\")\n        \n        original_stdin = sys.stdin\n        original_stdout = sys.stdout\n        \n        # Simulate stdin and capture stdout\n        sys.stdin = StringIO(\"My name is Joey. I like Python.\\n\")\n        captured_stdout = StringIO()\n        \n        try:\n            with redirect_stdout(captured_stdout):\n                cli_custom_vowels = CLIController()\n                exit_code = cli_custom_vowels.run(['--vowels', 'aey'])\n            \n            print(f\"CLI exit code: {exit_code}\")\n            if exit_code == 0:\n                print(f\"Output content: '{captured_stdout.getvalue().strip()}'\\n\")\n            else:\n                print(\"CLI failed.\\n\")\n        finally:\n            sys.stdin = original_stdin\n            sys.stdout = original_stdout\n\n        # 3. CLI: Large file processing with a specific chunk size\n        print(f\"3. CLI: Large file -> stdout (chunk_size={DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE * 2})\")\n\n        original_stdout = sys.stdout\n        captured_stdout_large = StringIO()\n        try:\n            with redirect_stdout(captured_stdout_large):\n                cli_large = CLIController()\n                exit_code = cli_large.run(['-i', large_input_file_path, '--chunk-size', str(DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE * 2)])\n            \n            print(f\"CLI exit code: {exit_code}\")\n            if exit_code == 0:\n                expected_output_prefix = (\"B\" * 1000 + \"\\n\" + \"C\" * 1000 + \"\\n\" + \"D\" * 1000 + \"F\" * 1000 + \"\\n\").strip()\n                actual_output_prefix = captured_stdout_large.getvalue().strip()[:len(expected_output_prefix)]\n                # print(f\"First part of output: '{actual_output_prefix}'\")\n                print(f\"Output length: {len(captured_stdout_large.getvalue().strip())} (expected much larger)\")\n                print(f\"Output starts as expected: {actual_output_prefix == expected_output_prefix}\\n\")\n            else:\n                print(\"CLI failed.\\n\")\n        finally:\n            sys.stdout = original_stdout\n\n\n        # 4. CLI: Error handling example (non-existent input file)\n        print(\"4. CLI: Error handling (non-existent input file)\")\n        original_stderr = sys.stderr\n        captured_stderr = StringIO()\n        try:\n            with redirect_stderr(captured_stderr):\n                cli_error = CLIController()\n                exit_code = cli_error.run(['-i', 'non_existent_file.txt'])\n            \n            print(f\"CLI exit code: {exit_code}\")\n            print(f\"Error output: '{captured_stderr.getvalue().strip()}'\\n\")\n        finally:\n            sys.stderr = original_stderr\n\n    finally:\n        # Clean up dummy files\n        if os.path.exists(input_file_path):\n            os.remove(input_file_path)\n        if os.path.exists(output_file_path):\n            os.remove(output_file_path)\n        if os.path.exists(large_input_file_path):\n            os.remove(large_input_file_path)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run_library_examples()\n    run_cli_examples()\n```"}
