{"task_id": "HumanEval/54", "solution": "def same_chars(s0: str, s1: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if two words have the same unique characters, ignoring order and multiplicity.\n    Compares the set of unique characters in s0 with the set of unique characters in s1.\n    >>> same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzzzddeddabc')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('abcd', 'dddddddabc')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('dddddddabc', 'abcd')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('eabcd', 'dddddddabc')\n    False\n    >>> same_chars('abcd', 'dddddddabce')\n    False\n    >>> same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzzzddddabc')\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    return set(s0) == set(s1)"}
