{"task_id": "HumanEval/67", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef fruit_distribution(s, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of mango fruits in a basket given a string describing apples and oranges\n    and the total number of fruits.\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_s = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", s.strip().lower())\n\n    apple_count = 0\n    orange_count = 0\n\n    apple_match = re.search(r\"(\\d+)\\s*apples?\", normalized_s)\n    if apple_match:\n        apple_count = int(apple_match.group(1))\n\n    orange_match = re.search(r\"(\\d+)\\s*oranges?\", normalized_s)\n    if orange_match:\n        orange_count = int(orange_match.group(1))\n\n    mango_count = n - apple_count - orange_count\n    return mango_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/67", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef fruit_distribution(s, n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of mango fruits in a basket given apple and orange counts in a string and the total fruit count.\n    This function parses the counts from the input string and subtracts them from the total.\n    \"\"\"\n    pattern = re.compile(r\"(\\d+)\\s*apples?\\s*and\\s*(\\d+)\\s*oranges?\", re.I)\n    match = pattern.search(s)\n    \n    # Assuming valid input string format as per critical requirements (trust caller's inputs).\n    apples = int(match.group(1))\n    oranges = int(match.group(2))\n    \n    return n - apples - oranges\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/68", "solution": "```python\ndef pluck(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Selects the smallest even-valued node and its index from an array of non-negative integers.\n    If no even values or the array is empty, returns an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    smallest_even_value = None\n    smallest_even_index = -1\n\n    for i, value in enumerate(arr):\n        if value % 2 == 0:  # Check if the value is even\n            if smallest_even_value is None or value < smallest_even_value:\n                smallest_even_value = value\n                smallest_even_index = i\n\n    if smallest_even_value is None:\n        return []\n    else:\n        return [smallest_even_value, smallest_even_index]\n```"}
