{"task_id": "HumanEval/100", "solution": "def make_a_pile(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, you have to make a pile of n levels of stones.\n    The first level has n stones, and each subsequent level uses the next integer\n    with the same parity as the first level.\n    \"\"\"\n    levels = [n]\n    current_level_stones = n\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        current_level_stones += 2\n        levels.append(current_level_stones)\n    return levels"}
