{"task_id": "HumanEval/105", "solution": "def by_length(arr):\n    \"\"\"Given an array of integers, filters for values 1-9, sorts them ascending, reverses the result, then maps to English digit names.\n    Non-integer values and integers outside 1-9 are ignored.\"\"\"\n    \n    DIGIT_NAME_MAP = {\n        1: \"One\", 2: \"Two\", 3: \"Three\", 4: \"Four\", 5: \"Five\",\n        6: \"Six\", 7: \"Seven\", 8: \"Eight\", 9: \"Nine\"\n    }\n\n    # Filter for integers between 1 and 9 (inclusive)\n    filtered_ints = [x for x in arr if isinstance(x, int) and 1 <= x <= 9]\n    \n    # Sort the filtered integers in ascending order\n    sorted_ints = sorted(filtered_ints)\n    \n    # Reverse the sorted list\n    reversed_ints = list(reversed(sorted_ints))\n    \n    # Map each digit to its corresponding English name\n    result_names = [DIGIT_NAME_MAP[digit] for digit in reversed_ints]\n    \n    return result_names"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/105", "solution": "```python\ndef by_length(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms an array of integers into an ordered list of English digit names.\n    It filters for digits 1-9, sorts, reverses, and then maps to names.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Define the mapping for digits 1-9 as a local constant.\n    DIGIT_NAME_MAP = {\n        1: \"One\", 2: \"Two\", 3: \"Three\", 4: \"Four\", 5: \"Five\",\n        6: \"Six\", 7: \"Seven\", 8: \"Eight\", 9: \"Nine\"\n    }\n\n    # Step 1: Filter only integer-like values in the inclusive range 1..9.\n    # This process implicitly ignores non-numeric inputs or non-integer floats by comparison and value check.\n    filtered_digits = []\n    for x in arr:\n        if 1 <= x <= 9:\n            # Check if the numeric value is an integer (e.g., 2 or 2.0, but not 3.5).\n            if int(x) == x:\n                filtered_digits.append(int(x))\n    \n    # Step 2: Sort the filtered integers in ascending order.\n    filtered_digits.sort()\n\n    # Step 3: Reverse the sorted list to get descending order.\n    filtered_digits.reverse()\n\n    # Step 4: Map each integer to its corresponding English name.\n    result_names = [DIGIT_NAME_MAP[digit] for digit in filtered_digits]\n\n    return result_names\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/106", "solution": "```python\n# src/factorlist/__init__.py\nfrom .controller import APIController\nfrom .service import NumberProcessorService\nfrom .calculators import FactorialCalculator, SumCalculator\nfrom .repository import ListRepository\nfrom .config import Config\n\n_default_config = Config()\n# Initialize repository only if persistence is enabled to avoid file creation if not needed\n_default_repo = ListRepository(_default_config.persist_path) if _default_config.persist_enabled else None\n_default_service = NumberProcessorService(\n    factorial=FactorialCalculator(),\n    summer=SumCalculator(),\n    repo=_default_repo,\n    config=_default_config,\n)\n_default_controller = APIController(_default_service)\n\ndef compute_list(n: int, persist: bool = None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Top-level API function to compute the list based on n.\n    Delegates to the configured APIController.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _default_controller.compute_list(n, persist)\n\n# This is the `f(n)` function required by the original problem statement.\n# It delegates to the designed system's top-level programmatic API,\n# ensuring it meets the \"EXACT function name\" requirement while\n# still leveraging the implemented design.\ndef f(n):\n    \"\"\" Implement the function f that takes n as a parameter,\n    and returns a list of size n, such that the value of the element at index i is the factorial of i if i is even\n    or the sum of numbers from 1 to i otherwise.\n    i starts from 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    return compute_list(n, persist=False) # The original f(n) did not mention persistence, so disable by default.\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/config.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\nDEFAULT_PERSIST_PATH: str = \"factorlist_results.json\"\nPERSIST_ENABLED: bool = True\n\n@dataclass\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"Central configuration for the application.\"\"\"\n    persist_enabled: bool = PERSIST_ENABLED\n    persist_path: str = DEFAULT_PERSIST_PATH\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/exceptions.py\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input values.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass PersistenceError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for errors during data persistence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass ControllerError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Generic exception for controller-level failures.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/models.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nclass NumberResult:\n    \"\"\"Data Transfer Object for persisted number sequence results.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n: int, values: List[int], timestamp: str):\n        self.n = n\n        self.values = values\n        self.timestamp = timestamp\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Serializes the NumberResult object to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"n\": self.n,\n            \"values\": self.values,\n            \"timestamp\": self.timestamp,\n        }\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_dict(data: dict) -> 'NumberResult':\n        \"\"\"Creates a NumberResult object from a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return NumberResult(\n            n=data[\"n\"],\n            values=data[\"values\"],\n            timestamp=data[\"timestamp\"],\n        )\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/calculators.py\nclass FactorialCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a given integer.\"\"\"\n    def compute(self, i: int) -> int:\n        if i < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"i must be >= 0 for factorial calculation\")\n        result = 1\n        for k in range(2, i + 1):\n            result *= k\n        return result\n\nclass SumCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of integers from 1 to a given integer.\"\"\"\n    def compute(self, i: int) -> int:\n        if i < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"i must be >= 0 for sum calculation\")\n        return i * (i + 1) // 2\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/repository.py\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport os\n\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\nfrom .models import NumberResult\n\n# Configure a logger for the repository\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n# Basic handler for console output if not configured elsewhere\nif not logger.handlers:\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\nclass ListRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages persistence of NumberResult objects to a JSON file.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, path: str):\n        self._file_path = Path(path)\n\n    def save_list(self, n: int, values: List[int]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a new NumberResult record to the JSON file.\"\"\"\n        new_result = NumberResult(n=n, values=values, timestamp=datetime.now().isoformat())\n        \n        # Read existing data or initialize as empty list\n        records = []\n        if self._file_path.exists():\n            try:\n                with self._file_path.open('r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                    content = f.read()\n                    if content: # Handle empty file case\n                        records = json.loads(content)\n                    if not isinstance(records, list): # Ensure it's a list\n                        records = [records] # Wrap non-list content in a list\n            except (IOError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n                logger.warning(f\"Could not read existing persistence file {self._file_path}: {e}. Starting with empty records.\")\n                records = [] # Start fresh if file is corrupt or unreadable\n\n        records.append(new_result.to_dict())\n\n        # Atomic write to prevent file corruption\n        temp_file_path = self._file_path.with_suffix(\".json.tmp\")\n        try:\n            with temp_file_path.open('w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                json.dump(records, f, indent=2)\n            os.replace(temp_file_path, self._file_path)\n        except IOError as e:\n            if temp_file_path.exists():\n                temp_file_path.unlink() # Clean up temp file on error\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to save results to {self._file_path}: {e}\")\n\n    def load_last(self, n: Optional[int] = None) -> Optional[NumberResult]:\n        \"\"\"Loads the last saved NumberResult, optionally filtered by n.\"\"\"\n        if not self._file_path.exists():\n            return None\n        \n        try:\n            with self._file_path.open('r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                content = f.read()\n                if not content:\n                    return None\n                records = json.loads(content)\n            \n            if not isinstance(records, list):\n                records = [records] # Treat single object as a list of one\n\n            if n is not None:\n                # Find the last record matching n\n                for record_dict in reversed(records):\n                    if record_dict.get(\"n\") == n:\n                        return NumberResult.from_dict(record_dict)\n            else:\n                # Return the very last record\n                if records:\n                    return NumberResult.from_dict(records[-1])\n            return None\n\n        except (IOError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to load results from {self._file_path}: {e}\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/service.py\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .calculators import FactorialCalculator, SumCalculator\nfrom .repository import ListRepository\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, PersistenceError\n\n# Configure a logger for the service\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\nif not logger.handlers:\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\nclass NumberProcessorService:\n    \"\"\"Business logic for computing number sequences and orchestrating persistence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        factorial: FactorialCalculator,\n        summer: SumCalculator,\n        repo: Optional[ListRepository],\n        config: Config\n    ):\n        self._factorial = factorial\n        self._summer = summer\n        self._repo = repo\n        self._config = config\n\n    def compute_sequence(self, n: int, persist: Optional[bool] = None) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the sequence of numbers f(n) and optionally persists the result.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if n is less than 1.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be an integer >= 1\")\n\n        result = []\n        for i in range(1, n + 1): # 1-based indexing for rule evaluation\n            if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index\n                val = self._factorial.compute(i)\n            else:  # Odd index\n                val = self._summer.compute(i)\n            result.append(val)\n\n        # Determine persistence behavior\n        do_persist = persist if persist is not None else self._config.persist_enabled\n        if do_persist and self._repo is not None:\n            try:\n                self._repo.save_list(n, result)\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                # Fail-soft: log the error but do not re-raise or block computation result\n                logger.error(f\"Persistence failed for n={n}: {e}. Computation result still returned.\")\n        \n        return result\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/controller.py\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .service import NumberProcessorService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, ControllerError\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles external API requests, validates input, and delegates to the service layer.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: NumberProcessorService):\n        self._service = service\n\n    def compute_list(self, n: int, persist: Optional[bool] = None) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Public API method to compute the number sequence.\n        Performs basic input validation before delegating to the service.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n        if n < 1:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (n >= 1).\")\n        \n        try:\n            return self._service.compute_sequence(n, persist)\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            # Propagate specific input errors\n            raise e\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Wrap unexpected internal errors\n            raise ControllerError(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/cli.py\nimport sys\nimport argparse\nimport json\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .controller import APIController\nfrom .service import NumberProcessorService\nfrom .calculators import FactorialCalculator, SumCalculator\nfrom .repository import ListRepository\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, ControllerError\n\nclass CLIApp:\n    \"\"\"Command-Line Interface application for factorlist.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, controller: APIController):\n        self._controller = controller\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses arguments and executes the main CLI logic.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Compute a special number sequence: factorial for even indices, sum for odd.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"n\", \n            type=int, \n            help=\"The length of the list to generate (n >= 1).\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--no-persist\", \n            action=\"store_true\", \n            help=\"Do not persist the computed results to disk.\"\n        )\n\n        try:\n            args = parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n            \n            n = args.n\n            persist = not args.no_persist if args.no_persist else None # Use None to defer to default config\n\n            result = self._controller.compute_list(n, persist=persist)\n            print(json.dumps(result))\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Invalid input: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except ControllerError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: An application error occurred: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error: An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the CLI script.\"\"\"\n    # Dependency injection setup for CLI\n    app_config = Config()\n    app_repo = ListRepository(app_config.persist_path) if app_config.persist_enabled else None\n    app_service = NumberProcessorService(\n        factorial=FactorialCalculator(),\n        summer=SumCalculator(),\n        repo=app_repo,\n        config=app_config\n    )\n    app_controller = APIController(app_service)\n    cli_app = CLIApp(app_controller)\n    sys.exit(cli_app.run(sys.argv))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n```python\n# src/factorlist/utils.py\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef validate_positive_int(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if a string can be converted to an integer >= 1.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if validation fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        n = int(s)\n        if n < 1:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Value '{s}' must be a positive integer (>= 1).\")\n        return n\n    except ValueError:\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Value '{s}' is not a valid integer.\")\n\n```\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"factorlist\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python application for computing and optionally persisting a specialized number sequence.\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nkeywords = [\"factorial\", \"sum\", \"cli\", \"python\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Development Status :: 3 - Alpha\",\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/factorlist\"\nDocumentation = \"https://github.com/yourusername/factorlist/blob/main/README.md\"\nRepository = \"https://github.com/yourusername/factorlist.git\"\n\n[project.scripts]\nfactorlist = \"factorlist.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/106", "solution": "def f(n):\n    \"\"\"Implement the function f to return a sequence list.\n    Elements are factorial(i) for even i, or sum(1..i) for odd i.\n    \"\"\"\n    _factorial_cache = {0: 1, 1: 1} # Cache for factorials during this run.\n\n    def _calculate_factorial(num):\n        # Calculate factorial of num, leveraging _factorial_cache for efficiency.\n        if num in _factorial_cache:\n            return _factorial_cache[num]\n\n        # Determine start point for calculation from cache\n        current_fact = 1\n        start_j = 1\n        # Find the largest cached value less than num to start multiplication from.\n        for k_val in sorted(_factorial_cache.keys(), reverse=True):\n            if k_val < num:\n                start_j = k_val + 1\n                current_fact = _factorial_cache[k_val]\n                break\n\n        for j in range(start_j, num + 1):\n            current_fact *= j\n            _factorial_cache[j] = current_fact # Cache intermediate results.\n        return current_fact\n\n    def _calculate_sum_to(num):\n        # Calculate the sum of numbers from 1 to num using the arithmetic series formula.\n        return num * (num + 1) // 2\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1): # i is the 1-based index.\n        if i % 2 == 0: # If i is even, use factorial.\n            result.append(_calculate_factorial(i))\n        else: # If i is odd, use sum.\n            result.append(_calculate_sum_to(i))\n    return result"}
