{"task_id": "HumanEval/121", "solution": "def solution(lst):\n    \"\"\"Given a non-empty list of integers, return the sum of all of the odd elements that are in even positions.\n    Indexing is 0-based.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for index, element in enumerate(lst):\n        # Add the element to the sum if its index is even and the element itself is odd.\n        if index % 2 == 0 and element % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum += element\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/121", "solution": "```\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"oddindexsum\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A small library and CLI to sum odd integers at even indices.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nkeywords = [\"sum\", \"odd\", \"even\", \"cli\", \"library\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Topic :: Utilities\"\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/oddindexsum\"\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/yourusername/oddindexsum/issues\"\n\n[project.scripts]\noddindexsum = \"oddindexsum.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\npythonpath = [\"src\"]\naddopts = \"--strict-markers\"\n\n[tool.black]\nline-length = 120\ntarget-version = ['py38']\n\n[tool.isort]\nprofile = \"black\"\nline_length = 120\nknown_first_party = [\"oddindexsum\"]\n```\n\n```\n# requirements.txt\npytest>=7.0.0\n```\n\n```\n# README.md\n# oddindexsum\n\nA small Python library and command-line interface (CLI) to compute the sum of odd integers located at even indices in a non-empty list of integers.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Library Function**: A Python function `SumService.sum_odd_at_even_positions` to integrate into other applications.\n- **CLI Tool**: An `oddindexsum` command-line tool for quick calculations.\n- **Robust Input Validation**: Handles various invalid inputs gracefully.\n- **Unit Tested**: Comprehensive unit and integration tests covering edge cases.\n- **Modular Design**: Suitable for packaging and CI/CD pipelines.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install `oddindexsum` using pip:\n\n```bash\npip install oddindexsum\n```\n\nTo install from source for development:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/oddindexsum.git\ncd oddindexsum\npip install -e .\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\nYou can use the `SumService` directly in your Python code:\n\n```python\nfrom oddindexsum import SumService, Validator, InvalidInputError\n\nservice = SumService()\nvalidator = Validator()\n\ntry:\n    my_list = [5, 8, 7, 1]\n    validator.validate_list(my_list) # Optional: validate first if input is untrusted\n    result = service.sum_odd_at_even_positions(my_list)\n    print(f\"The sum is: {result}\") # Output: The sum is: 12\n\n    my_list_negatives = [-5, 2, -7, 10, 1]\n    validator.validate_list(my_list_negatives)\n    result_neg = service.sum_odd_at_even_positions(my_list_negatives)\n    print(f\"The sum with negatives is: {result_neg}\") # Output: The sum with negatives is: -12\nexcept InvalidInputError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\n### CLI\n\nThe `oddindexsum` command-line tool accepts integers as arguments or a JSON list via argument or stdin.\n\n**1. Space-separated integers as arguments:**\n\n```bash\noddindexsum 5 8 7 1\n# Output: 12\n```\n\n**2. A single argument as a JSON list:**\n\n```bash\noddindexsum \"[3,3,3,3,3]\"\n# Output: 9\n```\n\n**3. JSON list via standard input (stdin):**\n\n```bash\necho \"[30, 13, 24, 321]\" | oddindexsum\n# Output: 0\n```\n\n**Error Handling:**\n\nInvalid inputs will result in an error message printed to `stderr` and an exit code of `2`.\n\n```bash\noddindexsum 1 2 \"hello\" 4\n# Output (to stderr): Invalid input: Element at index 2 is not int: hello\n# Exit code: 2\n```\n\n```bash\noddindexsum\n# Output (to stderr): Invalid input: No input provided\n# Exit code: 2\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\nTo run the unit and integration tests, navigate to the project root and execute `pytest`:\n\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 oddindexsum/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 sum_service.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 validator.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 input_list.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 result.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 cli.py\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_sum_service.py\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_validator.py\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 test_cli.py\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 .github/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 workflows/\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 ci.yml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 requirements.txt\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md\n```\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License - see the LICENSE file for details (if applicable, otherwise state MIT in `pyproject.toml`).\n```\n\n```\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n      - develop\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n      - develop\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.8\", \"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\", \"3.12\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        python -m pip install --upgrade pip\n        pip install -r requirements.txt\n        pip install -e . # Install package in editable mode for testing\n    - name: Lint with Black\n      run: |\n        pip install black\n        black --check .\n    - name: Lint with isort\n      run: |\n        pip install isort\n        isort --check-only .\n    - name: Run tests with pytest\n      run: |\n        pytest\n```\n\n```python\n# src/oddindexsum/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\noddindexsum package exports.\nExposes core services, DTOs, and exceptions for easy access.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .cli import CLI\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .input_list import InputList\nfrom .result import Result\nfrom .sum_service import SumService\nfrom .validator import Validator\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"CLI\",\n    \"InvalidInputError\",\n    \"InputList\",\n    \"Result\",\n    \"SumService\",\n    \"Validator\",\n]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/oddindexsum/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nDefines custom exception types for domain-specific errors.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised for invalid input to the sum computation service or CLI.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n```\n\n```python\n# src/oddindexsum/input_list.py\n\"\"\"\nInputList DTO for wrapping a list of integers.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Any, List, Sequence\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass InputList:\n    \"\"\"\n    A Data Transfer Object (DTO) for wrapping a list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    items: List[int]\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_sequence(cls, seq: Sequence[Any]) -> \"InputList\":\n        \"\"\"\n        Factory method to create an InputList from a sequence.\n        Assumes sequence has been validated to contain only integers.\n        \"\"\"\n        return cls(list(seq))\n```\n\n```python\n# src/oddindexsum/result.py\n\"\"\"\nResult DTO for encapsulating the integer computation result.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Result:\n    \"\"\"\n    A Data Transfer Object (DTO) for wrapping the integer result.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    value: int\n```\n\n```python\n# src/oddindexsum/sum_service.py\n\"\"\"\nCore computation service for summing odd integers at even positions.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .input_list import InputList\nfrom .result import Result\n\n\nclass SumService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides the core business logic for summing odd integers at even positions.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the SumService. This service is stateless.\n        \"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def sum_odd_at_even_positions(self, lst: List[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the sum of odd elements located at even positions (0-based) in a list.\n        Precondition: `lst` is a non-empty list of integers.\n        \"\"\"\n        total = 0\n        for idx, val in enumerate(lst):\n            # Check if index is even and value is odd (negative odds count)\n            if idx % 2 == 0 and abs(val) % 2 == 1:\n                total += val\n        return total\n\n    def sum_from_input(self, input_dto: InputList) -> Result:\n        \"\"\"\n        Convenience method to compute the sum using an InputList DTO.\n        \"\"\"\n        return Result(self.sum_odd_at_even_positions(input_dto.items))\n```\n\n```python\n# src/oddindexsum/validator.py\n\"\"\"\nInput validation layer for the oddindexsum library and CLI.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any, Sequence\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n\nclass Validator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates input lists according to specified constraints.\n    Raises InvalidInputError for any validation failures.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the Validator. This validator is stateless.\n        \"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    def validate_list(self, lst: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates an input to ensure it is a non-empty sequence of integers.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if the input does not meet the criteria.\n        \"\"\"\n        if lst is None:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input is None\")\n        if not isinstance(lst, Sequence) or isinstance(lst, (str, bytes)):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a sequence of integers\")\n        if not lst:  # Check for empty sequence\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input sequence must be non-empty\")\n        for i, el in enumerate(lst):\n            if not isinstance(el, int):\n                raise InvalidInputError(f\"Element at index {i} is not int: {el}\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/oddindexsum/cli.py\n\"\"\"\nCLI entrypoint for the oddindexsum application.\nParses arguments, validates input, calls the service, and prints the result.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .sum_service import SumService\nfrom .validator import Validator\n\nEXIT_OK = 0\nEXIT_INVALID_INPUT = 2\n\n\nclass CLI:\n    \"\"\"\n    Command Line Interface (CLI) for the oddindexsum application.\n    Handles argument parsing, input validation, and result output.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, validator: Optional[Validator] = None, service: Optional[SumService] = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the CLI with optional dependency injection for Validator and SumService.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.validator = validator or Validator()\n        self.service = service or SumService()\n\n    def _parse_args(self, args: List[str]) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses command-line arguments or stdin into a list of integers.\n        Supports space-separated integers, a single JSON list argument, or JSON via stdin.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not args:\n            # No arguments, try reading from stdin\n            raw_input = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n            if not raw_input:\n                raise InvalidInputError(\"No input provided (arguments or stdin)\")\n            try:\n                parsed = json.loads(raw_input)\n                if isinstance(parsed, list):\n                    return parsed\n                raise InvalidInputError(\"Stdin must contain a JSON list of integers\")\n            except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n                raise InvalidInputError(f\"Invalid JSON from stdin: {e}\")\n\n        # Arguments are present\n        if len(args) == 1:\n            try:\n                # First try to parse as a JSON list\n                parsed = json.loads(args[0])\n                if isinstance(parsed, list):\n                    return parsed\n            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                pass  # Not a JSON list, fall through to space-separated\n        \n        # Fallback to parsing space-separated integers\n        try:\n            return [int(x) for x in args]\n        except ValueError as e:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Invalid integer argument found: {e}\")\n\n    def run(self, args: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Main CLI runner method. Parses inputs, performs computation, and prints result.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, 2 for invalid input).\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            input_args = args if args is not None else sys.argv[1:]\n            items = self._parse_args(input_args)\n            self.validator.validate_list(items)  # Validate the parsed list\n            result = self.service.sum_odd_at_even_positions(items)\n            print(result)\n            return EXIT_OK\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Invalid input: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return EXIT_INVALID_INPUT\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1  # General error exit code\n\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"\n    Entry point for the console script.\n    \"\"\"\n    cli = CLI()\n    sys.exit(cli.run())\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nUnit tests for the custom exception types.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom oddindexsum.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n\ndef test_invalid_input_error_message():\n    \"\"\"\n    Verifies that InvalidInputError correctly stores and retrieves its message.\n    \"\"\"\n    message = \"Test error message\"\n    e = InvalidInputError(message)\n    assert e.message == message\n    assert str(e) == message\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_input_list.py\n\"\"\"\nUnit tests for the InputList DTO.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom oddindexsum.input_list import InputList\n\n\ndef test_input_list_creation():\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests that InputList can be created with a list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    data = [1, 2, 3]\n    input_list = InputList(items=data)\n    assert input_list.items == data\n\n\ndef test_input_list_from_sequence():\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests the from_sequence factory method with different sequence types.\n    \"\"\"\n    seq_tuple = (4, 5, 6)\n    input_list_tuple = InputList.from_sequence(seq_tuple)\n    assert input_list_tuple.items == [4, 5, 6]\n\n    seq_list = [7, 8, 9]\n    input_list_list = InputList.from_sequence(seq_list)\n    assert input_list_list.items == [7, 8, 9]\n\n\ndef test_input_list_immutability():\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests that InputList is frozen (immutable).\n    \"\"\"\n    data = [1, 2, 3]\n    input_list = InputList(items=data)\n    try:\n        input_list.items = [4, 5, 6]  # type: ignore\n        assert False, \"InputList should be immutable (frozen)\"\n    except Exception:\n        assert True\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_result.py\n\"\"\"\nUnit tests for the Result DTO.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom oddindexsum.result import Result\n\n\ndef test_result_creation():\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests that Result can be created with an integer value.\n    \"\"\"\n    value = 123\n    result = Result(value=value)\n    assert result.value == value\n\n\ndef test_result_immutability():\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests that Result is frozen (immutable).\n    \"\"\"\n    result = Result(value=100)\n    try:\n        result.value = 200  # type: ignore\n        assert False, \"Result should be immutable (frozen)\"\n    except Exception:\n        assert True\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_sum_service.py\n\"\"\"\nUnit tests for the SumService class.\nCovers various scenarios including examples, edge cases, and negative numbers.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom oddindexsum.input_list import InputList\nfrom oddindexsum.result import Result\nfrom oddindexsum.sum_service import SumService\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef sum_service():\n    \"\"\"Provides a SumService instance for tests.\"\"\"\n    return SumService()\n\n\ndef test_examples(sum_service):\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests the provided examples from the problem description.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([5, 8, 7, 1]) == 12\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([3, 3, 3, 3, 3]) == 9\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([30, 13, 24, 321]) == 0\n\n\ndef test_negative_odd_numbers(sum_service):\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests lists containing negative odd numbers at even positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Index 0: -5 (odd) -> -5\n    # Index 2: -7 (odd) -> -7\n    # Total: -5 + -7 = -12\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([-5, 2, -7, 10, 1]) == -12\n    # Index 0: -1 (odd) -> -1\n    # Total: -1\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([-1, 0, 1, 0, 3]) == -1\n    # Index 0: -10 (even) -> 0\n    # Total: 0\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([-10, -13, -11, -12]) == 0\n\n\ndef test_mixed_positive_negative_odds(sum_service):\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests lists with mixed positive and negative odd numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Index 0: 5 (odd) -> 5\n    # Index 2: -7 (odd) -> -7\n    # Total: 5 + -7 = -2\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([5, 2, -7, 10, 1]) == -2\n\n\ndef test_no_odd_at_even_positions(sum_service):\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests lists where no odd numbers are found at even positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([2, 4, 6, 8, 10]) == 0\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([10, 11, 12, 13]) == 0\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([0, 0, 0, 0]) == 0\n\n\ndef test_single_element_list(sum_service):\n    \"\"\"\n    Tests lists with a single element.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert sum_service.sum_odd_at_even_positions([5]) == 5  # index 0 is 