{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "def do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates an algebraic expression from operator and operand lists respecting precedence.\n    Uses the shunting-yard algorithm for RPN conversion and RPN evaluation.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    OPERATOR_INFO = {\n        '**': {'precedence': 4, 'associativity': 'right'},\n        '*': {'precedence': 3, 'associativity': 'left'},\n        '//': {'precedence': 3, 'associativity': 'left'},\n        '+': {'precedence': 2, 'associativity': 'left'},\n        '-': {'precedence': 2, 'associativity': 'left'},\n    }\n\n    # Helper function for operator comparison used in shunting-yard.\n    def _should_pop_operator(op1_symbol, op2_symbol):\n        op1_info = OPERATOR_INFO[op1_symbol]\n        op2_info = OPERATOR_INFO[op2_symbol]\n\n        if op1_info['associativity'] == 'left':\n            return op1_info['precedence'] <= op2_info['precedence']\n        else:  # 'right' associativity\n            return op1_info['precedence'] < op2_info['precedence']\n\n    # 1. Interleave operands and operators into an infix token list.\n    infix_tokens = []\n    for i in range(len(operand)):\n        infix_tokens.append(operand[i])\n        if i < len(operator): # Add operator between operands\n            infix_tokens.append(operator[i])\n\n    # 2. Shunting-Yard Algorithm: Convert infix expression to Reverse Polish Notation (RPN).\n    output_queue = []\n    operator_stack = []\n\n    for token in infix_tokens:\n        if isinstance(token, int):  # Token is an operand\n            output_queue.append(token)\n        else:  # Token is an operator (string symbol)\n            while operator_stack and _should_pop_operator(token, operator_stack[-1]):\n                output_queue.append(operator_stack.pop())\n            operator_stack.append(token)\n\n    # Pop any remaining operators from the stack to the output queue.\n    while operator_stack:\n        output_queue.append(operator_stack.pop())\n\n    # 3. RPN Evaluation: Evaluate the RPN token list.\n    evaluation_stack = []\n\n    for token in output_queue:\n        if isinstance(token, int):  # Token is an operand\n            evaluation_stack.append(token)\n        else:  # Token is an operator (string symbol)\n            # Pop operands from the stack (right then left).\n            right = evaluation_stack.pop()\n            left = evaluation_stack.pop()\n            \n            # Apply the operator.\n            if token == '+':\n                result = left + right\n            elif token == '-':\n                result = left - right\n            elif token == '*':\n                result = left * right\n            elif token == '//':\n                result = left // right\n            elif token == '**':\n                result = left ** right\n            \n            evaluation_stack.append(result)\n            \n    # The final result is the single value remaining on the stack.\n    return evaluation_stack[0]"}
