{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# This file describes the project's metadata, dependencies, and build system.\n\n[project]\nname = \"strcaseapp\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reusable library to transform strings by reversing letter case or reversing entire string when no letters present.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nkeywords = [\"string-transformation\", \"cli\", \"api\", \"python\"]\nauthors = [\n  { name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" },\n]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Development Status :: 3 - Alpha\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.8\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.9\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Topic :: Text Processing\",\n    \"Topic :: Utilities\",\n]\n\n[project.dependencies]\n# No runtime dependencies beyond standard library for the core logic\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\napi = [\n    \"fastapi>=0.100.0\",\n    \"uvicorn[standard]>=0.20.0\",\n    \"pydantic>=2.0.0\" # Required by FastAPI\n]\n\n[project.scripts]\nstrcase = \"strcaseapp.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n```\n\n```python\n# README.md\n# strcaseapp\nA versatile Python library and application for string transformations. It reverses the case of alphabetic characters or, if no letters are present, reverses the entire string.\n\n## Features\n- **Library Function**: `strcaseapp.solve(text: str)` for programmatic use.\n- **CLI Tool**: `strcase` command for quick transformations from the terminal.\n- **HTTP API**: Optional FastAPI endpoint for integration (`POST /process`).\n- **Robust Error Handling**: Clear exceptions for invalid inputs.\n- **Testable Design**: Modular architecture for easy unit and integration testing.\n\n## Installation\n\n### Using pip\n```bash\npip install strcaseapp\n```\n\n### For CLI usage\nThe `strcase` command will be available after installation.\n\n### For HTTP API usage\nTo run the HTTP API, you need to install the `api` extra:\n```bash\npip install \"strcaseapp[api]\"\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### As a Library\n```python\nimport strcaseapp\n\n# Example 1: Letters present, case reversed\nprint(strcaseapp.solve(\"Hello World 123!\"))  # Output: hELLO wORLD 123!\n\n# Example 2: No letters present, string reversed\nprint(strcaseapp.solve(\"12345\"))             # Output: 54321\n\n# Example 3: Mixed characters\nprint(strcaseapp.solve(\"#a@B$c\"))            # Output: #A@b$C\n\n# Example 4: Empty string (no letters, reversed empty is empty)\nprint(strcaseapp.solve(\"\"))                  # Output: \"\"\n\n# Error handling\ntry:\n    strcaseapp.solve(None)\nexcept strcaseapp.InvalidInputError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\n### Via CLI\n```bash\nstrcase \"HelloWorld123\"\n# Output: hELLOwORLD123\n\nstrcase \"98765\"\n# Output: 56789\n\nstrcase \"#test!\"\n# Output: #TEST!\n\n# Use with --text option\nstrcase --text \"Another test\"\n# Output: aNOTHER TEST\n\n# Get help\nstrcase --help\n```\n\n### Via HTTP API (optional)\nFirst, ensure you have installed the `api` extra: `pip install \"strcaseapp[api]\"`.\nThen, run the API server (e.g., using uvicorn):\n```bash\nuvicorn strcaseapp.api:create_app --factory --reload --port 8000\n```\nThe API will be available at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`. You can send POST requests to `/process`.\n\nExample using `curl`:\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"text\": \"Sample Text 123\"}' http://127.0.0.1:8000/process\n# Expected output: {\"result\":\"sAMPLE tEXT 123\"}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"text\": \"09876\"}' http://127.0.0.1:8000/process\n# Expected output: {\"result\":\"67890\"}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"not_text_field\": \"oops\"}' http://127.0.0.1:8000/process\n# Expected output: {\"detail\":\"'text' field is required and must be a string.\"} (HTTP 400)\n```\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nstrcaseapp package exports.\nProvides the main solve function for programmatic use and version information.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, ProcessingError # noqa: F401\nfrom .services import StringProcessor\nfrom .models import ProcessRequest, ProcessResult # noqa: F401\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\n# Export the solve function for convenience\n_default_processor = StringProcessor()\n\ndef solve(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Solves the string transformation problem.\n    Reverses letter case or reverses the entire string if no letters are present.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _default_processor.solve(s)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/config.py\n\"\"\"\nConfiguration constants and defaults for the strcaseapp.\n\"\"\"\n\nDEFAULT_CHARSET: str = 'unicode'  # Informational, Python's str methods handle unicode by default\nCLI_PROG_NAME: str = 'strcase'\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/models.py\n\"\"\"\nData Transfer Objects (DTOs) for processing requests and results.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, ProcessingError\n\nclass ProcessRequest:\n    \"\"\"\n    Represents an input request for string processing.\n    Ensures input text is a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, text: str) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(text, str):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input for ProcessRequest must be a string.\")\n        self.text: str = text\n\nclass ProcessResult:\n    \"\"\"\n    Represents the result of string processing.\n    Holds the transformed string.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, result: str) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(result, str):\n            raise ProcessingError(\"Result of processing must be a string.\")\n        self.result: str = result\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nApplication-specific exceptions for strcaseapp.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised for invalid input data.\n    Corresponds to HTTP 400 or CLI non-zero exit code.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass ProcessingError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised for unexpected errors during string processing.\n    Corresponds to HTTP 500 or CLI non-zero exit code.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/utils.py\n\"\"\"\nLow-level utility functions for character checks and string manipulation.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass Utils:\n    \"\"\"\n    A utility class providing static methods for string operations.\n    Handles character checks and string reversal efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_letter(ch: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a character is an alphabetic letter.\n        Returns False for empty strings or strings longer than one character.\n        \"\"\"\n        return len(ch) == 1 and ch.isalpha()\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def has_any_letter(s: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if the string contains any alphabetic characters.\n        Iterates through the string to find any letter.\n        \"\"\"\n        for ch in s:\n            if Utils.is_letter(ch):\n                return True\n        return False\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Reverses the entire input string.\n        Uses Python's slicing for efficient reversal.\n        \"\"\"\n        return s[::-1]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/transformers.py\n\"\"\"\nEncapsulates logic for transforming character cases within a string.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Callable, Optional\nfrom .utils import Utils\nfrom .exceptions import ProcessingError\n\nclass CaseTransformer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles case flipping for individual characters and full string transformations.\n    Can be initialized with a custom alphabetic check function.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, alphabetic_check: Optional[Callable[[str], bool]] = None) -> None:\n        self._alphabetic_check = alphabetic_check if alphabetic_check is not None else Utils.is_letter\n\n    def flip_case(self, ch: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Flips the case of an alphabetic character; otherwise, returns it unchanged.\n        Requires a single character input.\n        \"\"\"\n        if len(ch) != 1:\n            raise ProcessingError(\"flip_case expects a single character string.\")\n        return ch.swapcase() if self._alphabetic_check(ch) else ch\n\n    def transform_letters(self, s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Iterates through a string, flipping the case of each alphabetic character.\n        Non-alphabetic characters remain as they are.\n        \"\"\"\n        transformed_chars = [self.flip_case(ch) for ch in s]\n        return \"\".join(transformed_chars)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/services.py\n\"\"\"\nCore business logic service for string processing.\nOrchestrates transformation rules based on input content.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .models import ProcessRequest, ProcessResult\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, ProcessingError\nfrom .transformers import CaseTransformer\nfrom .utils import Utils\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass StringProcessor:\n    \"\"\"\n    Processes strings according to business rules: reverse letter case,\n    or reverse the entire string if no letters are present.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, transformer: Optional[CaseTransformer] = None, utils: Optional[Utils] = None) -> None:\n        self._transformer = transformer if transformer is not None else CaseTransformer()\n        self._utils = utils if utils is not None else Utils()\n\n    def process(self, request: ProcessRequest) -> ProcessResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Processes a ProcessRequest, applying string transformation rules.\n        Validates input and handles cases with/without letters.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            text = request.text\n            if self._utils.has_any_letter(text):\n                result = self._transformer.transform_letters(text)\n            else:\n                result = self._utils.reverse_string(text)\n            return ProcessResult(result)\n        except InvalidInputError:\n            # Re-raise InvalidInputError directly if it came from ProcessRequest constructor\n            raise\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Catch other potential errors during processing\n            raise ProcessingError(f\"An unexpected error occurred during processing: {e}\") from e\n\n    def solve(self, s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Convenience method to process a string directly.\n        Wraps the input in a ProcessRequest and returns the processed string.\n        \"\"\"\n        request = ProcessRequest(s)\n        result = self.process(request)\n        return result.result\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/controllers.py\n\"\"\"\nInput/output handlers for CLI and HTTP API interactions.\nAdapts raw input/output to internal service calls.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\nfrom .services import StringProcessor\nfrom .models import ProcessRequest\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, ProcessingError\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages the command-line interface logic.\n    Parses arguments, calls the string processor, and prints results.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, processor: StringProcessor) -> None:\n        self._processor = processor\n\n    def run(self, text_input: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the CLI command logic for a given text.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for error).\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            request = ProcessRequest(text_input) # Input validation happens here\n            result_obj = self._processor.process(request)\n            print(result_obj.result)\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Specific exit code for invalid input\n        except ProcessingError as e:\n            print(f\"Processing error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # General processing error\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Catch-all for unforeseen issues\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages the HTTP API request and response handling.\n    Validates payload, calls the string processor, and formats the JSON response.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, processor: StringProcessor) -> None:\n        self._processor = processor\n\n    def process_payload(self, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Processes an HTTP payload dictionary.\n        Extracts 'text', calls the processor, and returns a result dictionary.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(payload, dict):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Request body must be a JSON object.\")\n        \n        text = payload.get(\"text\")\n        if not isinstance(text, str):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"'text' field is required and must be a string.\")\n        \n        request = ProcessRequest(text) # Input validation happens here\n        result_obj = self._processor.process(request)\n        return {\"result\": result_obj.result}\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/cli.py\n\"\"\"\nCommand-line interface entrypoint for strcaseapp.\nParses arguments and delegates processing to the CLIController.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Optional, List\n\nfrom .config import CLI_PROG_NAME\nfrom .services import StringProcessor\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the CLI application.\n    Parses command-line arguments and runs the CLIController.\n    \"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        prog=CLI_PROG_NAME,\n        description=\"Transforms a string by reversing letter case or reversing the entire string.\",\n        formatter_class=argparse.RawTextHelpFormatter\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"text\",\n        nargs=\"?\", # Makes the positional argument optional\n        help=\"The string to process. If not provided, use --text.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"-t\", \"--text\",\n        dest=\"text_option\", # Use a different dest to avoid conflict with positional 'text'\n        help=\"The string to process (alternative to positional argument).\"\n    )\n\n    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    input_text: Optional[str] = None\n    if args.text is not None:\n        input_text = args.text\n    elif args.text_option is not None:\n        input_text = args.text_option\n    \n    if input_text is None:\n        # If neither positional nor --text is provided, it's an error.\n        parser.print_help(sys.stderr)\n        return 2 # Indicate invalid arguments or missing required argument\n\n    processor = StringProcessor()\n    controller = CLIController(processor)\n    return controller.run(input_text)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strcaseapp/api.py\n\"\"\"\nFastAPI application factory for the HTTP API.\nExposes a POST /process endpoint for string transformation.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ValidationError\n\nfrom .services import StringProcessor\nfrom .controllers import APIController\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, ProcessingError\n\n# Pydantic model for request body validation (FastAPI specific)\nclass ProcessRequestPayload(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"\n    Pydantic model for validating the HTTP POST request body.\n    Ensures the 'text' field is a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    text: str\n\ndef create_app(processor: Optional[StringProcessor] = None) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates and configures a FastAPI application instance.\n    Registers the /process endpoint and sets up error handling.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Check if FastAPI is installed\n        import fastapi # noqa: F401\n    except ImportError:\n        raise ImportError(\n            \"FastAPI and Uvicorn are not installed. \"\n            \"Please install them using 'pip install \\\"strcaseapp[api]\\\"'.\"\n        )\n\n    app = FastAPI(\n        title=\"String Case Transformation API\",\n        description=\"Reverses letter case or reverses the entire string if no letters are present.\",\n        version=\"0.1.0\",\n    )\n\n    # Initialize processor and controller.\n    # If processor is not provided, create a default one.\n    if processor is None:\n        processor = StringProcessor()\n    api_controller = APIController(processor)\n\n    @app.post(\"/process\", summary=\"Process a string\", response_model=dict)\n    async def process_string(payload_model: ProcessRequestPayload):\n        \"\"\"\n        HTTP POST endpoint to process a string.\n        Accepts JSON `{\"text\": \"your string\"}` and returns `{\"result\": \"processed string\"}`.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            # Pydantic model automatically validates and ensures 'text' is str\n            payload_dict = payload_model.model_dump()\n            result_dict = api_controller.process_payload(payload_dict)\n            return result_dict\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            # Pydantic validation errors map to 400 Bad Request\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=f\"Invalid request data: {e.errors()}\")\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e))\n        except ProcessingError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=f\"Internal processing error: {e}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Catch any other unforeseen errors\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=f\"An unexpected server error occurred: {e}\")\n\n    return app\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # This block is for local development with uvicorn.\n    # In production, you'd typically use `uvicorn strcaseapp.api:create_app --factory`.\n    try:\n        import uvicorn\n        app = create_app()\n        uvicorn.run(app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000)\n    except ImportError as e:\n        print(f\"Cannot run API directly: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        print(\"Please ensure FastAPI, Uvicorn, and Pydantic are installed ('pip install \\\"strcaseapp[api]\\\"').\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred while running the API: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_utils.py\n# Unit tests for Utils and CaseTransformer will go here.\n# (Content omitted as per CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS: \"FORBIDDEN: DO NOT write unit tests\")\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_services.py\n# Unit tests for StringProcessor will go here.\n# (Content omitted as per CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS: \"FORBIDDEN: DO NOT write unit tests\")\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_cli.py\n# Integration tests for CLI will go here.\n# (Content omitted as per CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS: \"FORBIDDEN: DO NOT write unit tests\")\n```"}
